update public.tips set body_md = '**Hoy laburo**, **ayer laburé**. The same verb: the ending changes and the stress jumps to it. *la-BU-ro* is now, *la-bu-RÉ* is done. Say it out loud and the past is already right.' where id = '37a39f47-ed41-5d5e-90c1-0134d9bbdc08' and body_md = '**Hoy laburo**, **ayer laburé**. The same verb, and only the stress moves: *la-BU-ro* is now, *la-bu-RÉ* is done. Say it out loud and the past is already right.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Fui** is both *I went* (ir) and *I was* (ser); **fue** is both *he went* and *it was*. **Fui a la cancha** — *I went to the game*; **fue re lindo** — *it was really nice*. The sentence always tells you which.' where id = '575cb41d-92ef-5b02-b25e-72e5a15b2ea0' and body_md = '**Fui** is both *I went* (ir) and *I was* (ser). **Fui a la cancha** — *I went to the game*; **fue re lindo** — *it was really nice*. The sentence always tells you which.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | estar | tener | pasarla |
| yo | estuve | tuve | **la pasé** |
| vos | estuviste | tuviste | **la pasaste** |
| él, ella | estuvo | tuvo | **la pasó** |
| nosotros | **estuvimos** | **tuvimos** | **la pasamos** |
| ellos | **estuvieron** | **tuvieron** | **la pasaron** |
*Estar* and *tener* get an odd stem (*estuv-*, *tuv-*) for every person, with no accent. *Pasarla* is regular: **la pasé**, **la pasó** keep the accent. **¿Cómo estuvo?** — *how was it?* — **Estuvo increíble, la pasamos bárbaro.**' where id = '9f882e99-1bc8-5b88-90df-07108c33ca10' and body_md = '| | estar | tener | pasarla |
| yo | estuve | tuve | **la pasé** |
| vos | estuviste | tuviste | **la pasaste** |
| él, ella | estuvo | tuvo | **la pasó** |
| nosotros | **estuvimos** | **tuvimos** | **la pasamos** |
| ellos | **estuvieron** | **tuvieron** | **la pasaron** |
The odd stem stays for every person, with no accent. **¿Cómo estuvo?** — *how was it?* — **Estuvo increíble, la pasamos bárbaro.**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cenamos** and **salimos** look the same in the present and the past: *we have dinner* or *we had dinner*, *we go out* or *we went out*. A porteño never gets lost: **anoche**, **ayer**, **el sábado** — the time word does the work.' where id = '9f2c679d-71d9-54c9-8c34-e6bc1cf22a1b' and body_md = '**Cenamos** and **salimos** are both *today* and *yesterday*. A porteño never gets lost: **anoche**, **ayer**, **el sábado** — the time word does the work.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Viste** is *you saw*: **¿Viste el partido?** — *Did you see the game?* Porteños also add **¿viste?** at the end of a sentence to mean *you know?*: *Es re caro, ¿viste?*' where id = '9e470499-223a-5382-8475-2b677a8e1fde' and body_md = '*¿Viste?* is also just *you saw*: **¿Viste el partido?** — *Did you see the game?* — the same word porteños drop into every story to mean *you know?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | hacer | ver | decir | venir | poder |
