| vos | hiciste | viste | dijiste | viniste | pudiste |
| él, ella | hizo | vio | dijo | vino | pudo |
| nosotros | hicimos | vimos | | | |
A new stem, then *-e, -iste, -o*, with no accent — *hizo* is spelled with a *z*. *Ver* keeps it short: *vi, viste, vio*. No accent on any of them. Tell the story in order with **primero**, **entonces**, **al final**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | traer | querer | venir | poder |
| yo | traje | quise | vine | pude |
| vos | trajiste | quisiste | viniste | pudiste |
| él, ella | trajo | quiso | vino | pudo |
| nosotros | | | vinimos | pudimos |
| ellos | trajeron | | vinieron | pudieron |
Same endings as *hice*: *-e, -iste, -o, -imos, -ieron* — after a *j*, just *-eron*: **dijeron, trajeron**. **No vino nadie** — *nobody came*: after the verb, *nadie* still needs the *no*; in front, it doesn''t: *nadie trajo hielo*.' where id = '717a288c-7ce1-5678-95a9-fb667c3542bc' and body_md = '| | traer | querer | venir | poder |
| yo | traje | quise | vine | pude |
| vos | trajiste | quisiste | viniste | pudiste |
| él, ella | trajo | quiso | vino | pudo |
| nosotros | | | vinimos | pudimos |
| ellos | trajeron | | vinieron | pudieron |
Same endings as *hice*: *-e, -iste, -o, -imos, -ieron* — after a *j*, just *-eron*: **dijeron, trajeron**. **No vino nadie** — after the verb, *nadie* still needs the *no*; in front, it doesn''t: *nadie trajo hielo*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Two more with their own stem and no accent: **traje, trajiste, trajo** (brought) and **quise, quisiste, quiso** (wanted, tried). **Quise** is about one moment — *I tried to*; **no quise** — *I refused*. **Quise venir, pero no pude** — *I wanted to come but couldn''t* — is the porteño apology for a missed asado.' where id = '38bd929f-9d15-5f91-9679-cd20e1ac26fb' and body_md = 'Two more with their own stem and no accent: **traje, trajiste, trajo** (brought) and **quise, quisiste, quiso** (wanted, tried). **Quise venir, pero no pude** — *I wanted to come but couldn''t* — is the porteño apology for a missed asado.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Mejor** and **peor** never take *más*: **está mejor**, **fue peor**. Only a kind person can be **más buena** — *nicer*. For *really*, porteños say **re**: *re rico*; *-ísimo* turns it up further: **riquísimo**, **carísimo**.' where id = 'f14e675f-3b81-58ce-92bd-dc0406370194' and body_md = '**Mejor** and **peor** never take *más*: **está mejor**, **fue peor**. For *really*, porteños say **re**: *re rico*; *-ísimo* turns it up further: **riquísimo**, **carísimo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '*-ísimo* works on almost anything: **baratísimo**, **lindísima**, and even on *lejos*: **queda lejísimos** — *it''s really far away*. It''s Spanish everywhere; the everyday porteño *really* is still **re**: *re lindo*.' where id = '56a5e066-372b-51d5-87a3-d9b7c8977270' and body_md = '*-ísimo* works on almost anything: **baratísimo**, **lindísima**, and even on *lejos*: **queda lejísimos** — *it''s miles away*. It''s Spanish everywhere; the everyday porteño *really* is still **re**: *re lindo*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| the most | **el** barrio **más** tranquilo **de** la ciudad |
| the least | **la** calle **menos** ruidosa |
| the best, the worst | **el mejor** del mundo, **el peor** |
| really, very | lindo → **lindísimo**, barato → **baratísimo** |
| really far | lejos → **lejísimos** |

*El* or *la* matches the thing, and the group comes after **de**: *la más linda **de** la ciudad*.' where id = 'c14df833-4206-56a3-89cb-5a50e8d2057c' and body_md = '| the most | **el** barrio **más** tranquilo **de** la ciudad |
| the least | **la** calle **menos** ruidosa |
| the best, the worst | **el mejor** del mundo, **el peor** |
| really, very | lindo → **lindísimo**, barato → **baratísimo** |
| miles away | lejos → **lejísimos** |

*El* or *la* matches the thing, and the group comes after **de**: *la más linda **de** la ciudad*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The thing that hurts is the subject: **me duele la cabeza** — *my head hurts*, **me duelen los pies** — *my feet hurt*. The *me* says whose, so Spanish uses *la*, not *mi*. For someone else, name them with *a*: **a Juan le duele la espalda** — *Juan''s back hurts*.' where id = 'e09dc1af-b15b-5bb4-a301-1cf6109dfb09' and body_md = 'The thing that hurts is the subject: **me duele la cabeza** — *my head hurts*, **me duelen los pies** — *my feet hurt*. The *me* says whose, so Spanish uses *la*, not *mi*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '*Doler* has a past too, and it stays glued to its *me*: **me dolió la cabeza** — *my head hurt*, **¿te dolió?**, **a mi viejo le dolió la rodilla**. When more than one thing hurt, it''s **dolieron**, just like *me duelen*: **me dolieron los ojos** — *my eyes hurt*.' where id = '1ef9dc5b-0a2c-51f6-8072-8665cac9cd15' and body_md = '*Doler* has a past too, and it stays glued to its *me*: **me dolió la cabeza** — *my head hurt*, **¿te dolió?**, **a mi viejo le dolió la rodilla**. Two things hurting, two endings, just like *me duelen*: **me dolieron los ojos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| him, or a masculine thing | **lo**, **los** | ¿El audio? **Lo** mando ahora. |
| her, or a feminine thing | **la**, **las** | ¿La tarjeta? **La** tengo. |
| to him, her, them | **le**, **les** | **Le** doy la llave. |
| me, you, us | **me**, **te**, **nos** | **Te** llamo mañana. |
Before a normal verb: *la tengo*. With a name you often say both: *lo llamo a Juan*, *les mando un audio a mis viejos*. Stuck to the end of a command, with no accent: **llamame**, **dame**, **mandame**, **prestame**.' where id = '863cc68c-e7da-5e85-9141-6c897afcf44b' and body_md = '| the thing, masculine | **lo**, **los** | ¿El audio? **Lo** mando ahora. |
| the thing, feminine | **la**, **las** | ¿La tarjeta? **La** tengo. |
| to him, her, them | **le**, **les** | **Le** doy la llave. |
| me, you | **me**, **te** | **Te** llamo mañana. |
Before a normal verb: *la tengo*. Stuck to the end of a command, with no accent: **llamame**, **dame**, **mandame**, **prestame**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Dar** has a short past with no accents: **di, diste, dio** — *le di la llave*. And *buscar* bends in *yo* to keep the hard *c* sound: **busqué** (not *buscé*).' where id = '7fd0a81b-3973-5a9c-8a43-62a122aa7461' and body_md = '**Dar** has a short past with no accents: **di, diste, dio** — *le di la llave*. And *buscar* bends in *yo* to keep the hard *c*: **busqué**, like *saqué*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me toca a mí** — *it''s my turn*. **¿A quién le toca?** — *whose turn is it?* The chore follows in its basic form (*lavar*, *sacar*, *limpiar*): **te toca lavar los platos**. Add *a mí* / *a vos* for stress: **hoy te toca a vos**.' where id = '35b971dd-87ee-5d40-9e55-ceb3b73004bc' and body_md = '**Me toca a mí** — *it''s my turn*. **¿A quién le toca?** — *whose turn is it?* The chore follows as it is: **te toca lavar los platos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The turn has a past: **ayer me tocó a mí, hoy te toca a vos**. **¿A quién le tocó?** Most chores are plain -ar verbs: **lavé, limpiaste, lavó**. *Sacar* changes in *yo*: **saqué** (like *busqué*). *Barrer* is an -er verb: **barrí, barriste**.' where id = 'acd8e9ee-2a6d-5a93-a00c-59315ddfc1b2' and body_md = 'The turn has a past: **ayer me tocó a mí, hoy te toca a vos**. **¿A quién le tocó?** And the chores are plain -ar verbs: **lavé, limpiaste, ordenó** — only *sacar* bends in *yo*: **saqué**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Holidays are told in *nosotros*: **alquilamos**, **nadamos**, **paseamos**, **sacamos mil fotos**. And the weather that ruined it: **llovió toda la semana**. In -ar verbs *nosotros* is the same now and in the past: **nadamos** is *we swim* or *we swam*; *ayer* or *en enero* tells you which.' where id = 'bd5cb236-10da-572d-bfd4-d7b1bf5ec6d4' and body_md = 'Holidays are told in *nosotros*: **alquilamos**, **nadamos**, **paseamos**, **sacamos mil fotos**. And the weather that ruined it: **llovió toda la semana**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me tocó** works like *gustar*: the thing is the subject, so with two things it is **me tocaron**: *me tocaron los platos y el baño*. **Llovió** has no person at all — just *it rained*.' where id = 'a160a37a-11e9-53de-a76b-fce48eb65bc8' and body_md = '**Me tocó** and **me dolió** work like *gustar*: the thing is the subject, so two things take *-eron*: **me dolieron los ojos**. **Llovió** has no person at all — just *it rained*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me toca lavar los platos** — *it''s my turn to do the dishes*. **¿A quién le toca?** Porteños say **me toca**, not *es mi turno*.' where id = '95be973e-2407-5c68-bc34-cf9e112dc823' and body_md = '**Me toca lavar** — *it''s my turn to do the dishes*. **¿A quién le toca?** Porteños split the chores with *tocar*, never with *turno*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Contame** opens it; **de repente** is the twist, **por suerte** the relief, **al final** the end. **Igual** — *anyway* — goes almost anywhere, and **o sea** is *I mean* or *so*.' where id = 'c3ebca78-c01d-5635-ae32-235914cc3de0' and body_md = '**Contame** opens it; **de repente** is the twist, **por suerte** the relief, **al final** the end. **Igual** — *anyway* — goes almost anywhere, and **o sea** is *I mean*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When the story ends badly, the answer is **¡Qué garrón!** — *how annoying!* Informal, and everywhere.' where id = 'c36061ee-ffa6-50e3-a2e5-06e46a8619e6' and body_md = 'When the story ends badly, the answer is **¡Qué garrón!** — *what a drag!* Informal, and everywhere.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | ser | tener | vivir | ir |
| yo, él, ella | era | tenía | vivía | iba |
| vos | eras | tenías | vivías | ibas |
| nosotros | éramos | | | íbamos |
This past describes: how things *were*, what you *had*, where you *lived*, what you *used to* do. *Yo* and *él* share one form — the story tells you which. **De chico** is *as a kid*: **De chico vivía en Rosario.** It changes with the person: **de chica** (a woman), **de chicos** (*we*).' where id = '862e703e-1590-5d4a-9240-1b3e1a058369' and body_md = '| | ser | tener | vivir | ir |
| yo, él, ella | era | tenía | vivía | iba |
| vos | eras | tenías | vivías | ibas |
| nosotros | éramos | | | íbamos |
This past describes: how things *were*, what you *had*, where you *lived*, what you *used to* do. *Yo* and *él* share one form — the story tells you which. **De chico** is *as a kid*: **De chico vivía en Rosario.**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In the past, *gustar* and *encantar* work like any -ar verb: **me gustaba**, **me encantaba** — *I liked*, *I loved*. Several things take an **-n**: **me gustaban los dibujitos**. *Ellos* too: **los pibes jugaban a la pelota en la vereda**.' where id = '9ec733ad-4e25-5b19-b479-b8f53e3f3e70' and body_md = '*Gustar* and *encantar* go back like any -ar verb: **me gustaba**, **me encantaba** — *I liked*, *I loved*. Several things take an **-n**: **me gustaban los dibujitos**. *Ellos* too: **los pibes jugaban a la pelota en la vereda**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | jugar | salir | ver |
| yo, él, ella | jug**aba** | sal**ía** | ve**ía** |
| vos | jug**abas** | sal**ías** | ve**ías** |
| nosotros | jug**ábamos** | sal**íamos** | ve**íamos** |
| ellos, ustedes | jug**aban** | sal**ían** | ve**ían** |
*Ver* keeps its *e*: **veía**. For TV, **miraba** and **veía** both work; to see a person, only *ver*: **veía a mi abuela**. **Me encantaba andar en bici.**' where id = 'df3230f6-6436-5eae-a43d-92ce8264bfcb' and body_md = '| | jugar | salir | ver |
| yo, él, ella | jug**aba** | sal**ía** | ve**ía** |
| vos | jug**abas** | sal**ías** | ve**ías** |
| nosotros | jug**ábamos** | sal**íamos** | ve**íamos** |
| ellos, ustedes | jug**aban** | sal**ían** | ve**ían** |
*Ver* keeps its *e*: **veía**. And *gustar* goes back like any -ar verb: **me gustaba** one thing, **me gustaban** several. **Me encantaba andar en bici.**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Había** is *there was, there were*; **hacía calor** is *it was hot*. **Estaba lloviendo** — *it was raining* — puts you in the middle of it; **llovía** says the same, and can also mean *it used to rain*. **Mientras** — *while* — joins two things going on at once.' where id = '636b7821-633f-5fb5-94b1-ae095af46302' and body_md = '**Había** is *there was, there were*; **hacía calor** is *it was hot*. **Estaba lloviendo** — *it was raining* — puts you in the middle of it. **Mientras** — *while* — joins two things going on at once.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Pedir** changes its vowel in some forms. Present: the *e* turns into *i* — **pido**. Past: **pedí** keeps the *e*, but for he or she it turns into *i* — **pidió**. **¿Qué pediste?** — **Pedí un bife.**' where id = '54958d4f-50e8-5d54-a404-928792675702' and body_md = '**Pedir** changes its vowel: **pido** today, **pedí** yesterday, and **pidió** for someone else. **¿Qué pediste?** — **Pedí un bife.**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Tipo** makes a time loose: **tipo ocho** is *around eight*, and in Buenos Aires people often arrive a bit later. For exactly eight, say **a las ocho en punto**.' where id = 'ed6072dc-6128-51a8-83b7-26e45cf6ccde' and body_md = '**Tipo** makes a time loose: **tipo ocho** is *around eight*, and in Buenos Aires that means eight-thirty. For exactly eight, say **a las ocho en punto**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me puse nervioso** — *I got nervous*; **se puso contenta** — *she was happy* (word for word: she got happy). The feeling changes, so it''s *ponerse*, in the preterite.' where id = 'c6f60906-d59e-542e-8047-b8fad681b872' and body_md = '**Me puse nervioso** — *I got nervous*; **se puso contenta** — *she got happy*. The feeling changes, so it''s *ponerse*, in the preterite.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Pronto** — *soon*; **a fin de año** — *at the end of the year*; **algún día** — *some day*. **¿Qué piensan hacer?** — **Pensamos juntar plata para viajar.** Careful: **pensar** + a verb is *to plan to*, but **pensar que** is *to think that*: *Juan piensa que tenés razón.* And the classic promise: **me anoté en el gimnasio**.' where id = '866c54a2-1f90-5dd1-9448-907edaf16201' and body_md = '**Pronto** — *soon*; **a fin de año** — *at the end of the year*; **algún día** — *some day*. **¿Qué piensan hacer?** — **Pensamos juntar plata para viajar.** Careful: **pensar** + a verb is *to plan to*, but **pensar que** is *to think that*: *Juan piensa que tenés razón.* And the classic January promise: **me anoté en el gimnasio**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me mudé** — *I moved (house)*; **nos mudamos** — *we moved*. The **mudanza** is the move itself, and always a *quilombo* (a mess).' where id = '72734c3b-aa10-5b4c-819d-56584b23250e' and body_md = '**Me mudé** — *I moved (house)*; **nos mudamos** — *we moved*. The **mudanza** is the move itself, and always a *quilombo*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'You rent through an **inmobiliaria** or straight from the **dueño**, and pay the **alquiler** every month. A **flete** takes the **muebles** and the **colchón**, and before unpacking, **pintamos**. And *they moved* is **se mudaron**.' where id = 'dbad321f-4d32-5c2e-9458-5dbbd5e6decf' and body_md = 'You rent through an **inmobiliaria** or straight from the **dueño**, and pay the **alquiler** every month. A **flete** takes the **muebles** and the **colchón**, and before unpacking, **pintamos**. The neighbors say it of you: **se mudaron**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The old place is imperfect, the move is preterite: **antes alquilaba en el centro** — how it was; **me mudé a Palermo** — what happened. **Extrañaba** is missing something over a period of time: *los primeros meses extrañaba mi barrio*.' where id = 'c7afa899-216a-57fc-be0d-9bbb58ad2055' and body_md = 'The old place is imperfect, the move is preterite: **antes alquilaba en el centro** — how it was; **me mudé a Palermo** — what happened. **Extrañaba** is missing that went on: *los primeros meses extrañaba mi barrio*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For plans, porteños use **voy a** + verb far more than the future: **la semana que viene voy a descansar**. **Pienso** + verb is also a plan: *I''m planning to*. **Tengo ganas de** is only wanting: *I feel like it*.' where id = '3e33b8ba-1526-5cde-95a7-43b8b9afcc60' and body_md = 'For plans, porteños use **voy a** + verb far more than the future: **la semana que viene voy a descansar**. **Pienso** and **tengo ganas de** do the same job.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'What you remember takes **de**: **mi abuela se acuerda de todo**; **nos acordamos de esa época**. Before **que** or **cuando**, people usually drop the **de**: *me acuerdo que íbamos a la playa*. **No me acordaba** — *I''d forgotten* — is imperfect: the not-remembering went on until someone brought it up.' where id = 'd68950b1-3362-55bb-81f3-e4f576a91d8e' and body_md = 'What you remember takes **de**: **mi abuela se acuerda de todo**; **nos acordamos de esa época**. **No me acordaba** — *I''d forgotten* — is imperfect: the not-remembering went on until someone brought it up.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A porteño asks with a plain question in the present: **¿me pasás la sal?**, **¿me ayudás?** — the *can you* is in the tone. **¿Podrías…?** is the extra-polite version. **¿Me pasás…?** and **¿me alcanzás…?** mean the same: *can you pass me…?*' where id = 'c5ccfebf-abb5-5c69-b2fb-f5a49cdb5788' and body_md = 'A porteño asks with a plain question in the present: **¿me pasás la sal?**, **¿me ayudás?** — the *can you* is in the tone. **¿Podrías…?** is the extra-polite version.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Tengo que laburar** is *I have to work*; **hay que** names no person — it just has to be done: **hay que sacar la basura** — *the trash has to go out*.' where id = '7fc50a6b-b755-5883-a742-eb3e04e4df87' and body_md = '**Tengo que laburar** is *I have to work*; **hay que** is the same for everyone: **hay que sacar la basura** — *the trash has to go out*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Drop the *no* and **hace falta** says what''s needed: **hace falta una fotocopia**. **¿Es obligatorio?** — *is it required?* — is a handy question at any counter.' where id = 'd621bc2e-5355-512b-b832-644c850667ef' and body_md = 'Drop the *no* and **hace falta** says what''s needed: **hace falta una fotocopia**. **¿Es obligatorio?** — *is it required?* — is the question every porteño asks at the counter.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Argentina has its own names: **palta** is avocado, **frutilla** is strawberry. Before you buy, ask **¿están maduras?** — *are they ripe?*' where id = 'fbd2133a-6859-5ead-9926-d782de4ed43e' and body_md = 'Buenos Aires has its own names: **palta** is avocado, **frutilla** is strawberry. Before you buy, ask **¿están maduras?** — *are they ripe?*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The vendor always asks **¿algo más?** — *anything else?* You answer **nada más, gracias**, or keep going: **y un kilo de naranjas**. To ask a price, **¿cuánto sale?** is the everyday way — same as *¿cuánto cuesta?*' where id = 'bbf8899a-9326-5028-a470-f2f170b9aab4' and body_md = 'The vendor always asks **¿algo más?** — *anything else?* You answer **nada más, gracias**, or keep going: **y un kilo de naranjas**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Tenés que llevar una fotocopia** — *you have to*; **hace falta una fotocopia** — *a photocopy is needed*, no person named; **no hace falta** — *there''s no need*.' where id = '75ad7c7e-3128-5ad9-82e3-98786bab822e' and body_md = '**Tenés que llevar una fotocopia** — someone has to; **hace falta una fotocopia** — something is needed; **no hace falta** — relax.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Me acompañás?** — the favor is for me; **¿nos sacás una foto?** — the favor is for us. It stays a question in the present — the tone does the asking.' where id = '4492bbdb-8376-566f-af0c-068e10d3456b' and body_md = '**¿Me acompañás?** asks for you; **¿nos sacás una foto?** asks for the two of you. It stays a question in the present — the tone does the asking.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The phone is **el celu** (short for *celular*). *Celular* is also the phone number: **pasame tu celular** — *give me your number*. **Me quedé sin batería** — *my battery died*; **se cortó** — *it cut out*; **mandame la ubicación** — *send me your location*. Without *sin*, **quedarse** is *to stay*: **¿te quedaste en casa?**' where id = '4e8246f2-31a4-5303-97f3-80f702ceb6f8' and body_md = 'The phone is **el celu** (short for *celular*). **Me quedé sin batería** — *my battery died*; **se cortó** — *it cut out*; **mandame la ubicación** — *send me your location*. Without *sin*, **quedarse** is *to stay*: **¿te quedaste en casa?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Tech orders are plain vos commands: **descargá la app**, **borrá las fotos**. What you already did is preterite: **la descargué**, **las borré**. In everyday speech you''ll also hear **bajar** for *download*: **bajate la app**.' where id = '6d7c070b-81b7-58f0-b526-20ee5f75be8d' and body_md = 'Tech orders are plain vos commands: **descargá la app**, **borrá las fotos**. What you already did is preterite: **la descargué**, **las borré**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Te devuelvo **el libro**. | Te **lo** devuelvo. |
| ¿Me dejás **las llaves**? | ¿Me **las** dejás? |
| Le regalé **un libro**. | **Se lo** regalé. |

The person goes first, the thing second. **Lo, la, los, las** match the thing: *el libro* → **lo**, *las llaves* → **las**. *Le* or *les* before them becomes **se**; add **a Sofi** to say who: **se la regalé a Sofi**.' where id = 'e310bbae-1d4a-5b28-99c7-88edb5d61f8a' and body_md = '| Te devuelvo **el libro**. | Te **lo** devuelvo. |
| ¿Me dejás **las llaves**? | ¿Me **las** dejás? |
| Le regalé **un libro**. | **Se lo** regalé. |

The person goes first, the thing second. *Le* or *les* before *lo, la* becomes **se**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Twice a year, in June and December, the **aguinaldo** arrives — half a month''s extra pay. Ask about it at the *entrevista*, along with the **licencia** — *paid leave* for a reason (sick, a new baby, exams). Your yearly holiday is **vacaciones**.' where id = '47214591-3206-5367-b7d5-e48af1764d9e' and body_md = 'Twice a year, in June and December, the **aguinaldo** arrives — half a month''s extra pay. Ask about it at the *entrevista*, along with the **licencia** — *paid leave*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Devolveme las llaves**, **dejame pasar**, **traeme el cargador** — in requests the pronoun rides on the end of the verb. Here it is *me*; for someone else it is *le*: **devolvele las llaves**.' where id = 'c975280b-817a-5375-b749-0900db51bc69' and body_md = '**Devolveme las llaves**, **dejame pasar**, **traeme el cargador** — in requests the pronoun rides on the end, and it''s always *me*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me quedé sin batería**, **sin plata**, **sin laburo** — *I ran out of*. It is the preterite: it happened at one moment. For how things were, use **tenía** and **estaba**: *estaba en el subte*, *no tenía plata*.' where id = 'c69d6cff-ff9d-5cb7-84a1-e7f685916f4c' and body_md = '**Me quedé sin batería**, **sin plata**, **sin laburo** — *I ran out of*. It is the preterite: it happened at one moment.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estoy saliendo con alguien** — *I''m seeing someone*. When it ends, porteños **cortan**: **cortamos** — *we broke up*. A fight is **nos peleamos** — *we had a fight* — or, for them, **se pelearon**. **Nos peleamos** is the same for now and for the past: *we fight* / *we had a fight*.' where id = 'dbb9fb4d-69cd-5b88-9d73-7d35bd390442' and body_md = '**Estoy saliendo con alguien** — *I''m seeing someone*. When it ends, porteños **cortan**: **cortamos** — *we broke up*. A fight is **nos peleamos** — *we had a fight* — or, for them, **se pelearon**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Qué hora será?** — *I wonder what time it is*. **Será** on its own shrugs: *could be*. **Capaz**, **quizás** and **seguro que** guess with the plain present: **capaz está en la plaza**; **seguro que es Juan**. In Buenos Aires you will hear **capaz** much more than **quizás**.' where id = '6f3c143b-2af0-5c70-b9e2-7435c2b347d4' and body_md = '**¿Qué hora será?** — *I wonder what time it is*. **Será** on its own shrugs: *could be*. **Capaz**, **quizás** and **seguro que** guess with the plain present: **capaz está en la plaza**; **seguro que es Juan**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Qué hará?** — *I wonder what he''s doing*; **¿cuánto costará?** — *I wonder how much it is*; **vendrá más tarde** — *she''ll probably come later*. For a group: **estarán en el bar**, **serán las ocho**. To vos: **¿estarás cansado?** — *you must be tired*.' where id = 'ce15b13a-f188-5034-9617-6e20515212c2' and body_md = '**¿Qué hará?** — *I wonder what he''s up to*; **¿cuánto costará?** — *I wonder how much it is*; **vendrá más tarde** — *she''ll probably come later*. For a group: **estarán en el bar**, **serán las ocho**. To vos: **¿estarás cansado?** — *you must be tired*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me siento mal** — *I feel sick*; **¿cómo te sentís?** — *how do you feel?* On its own, **lo siento** is *I''m sorry*. The vowel changes only when it is stressed: **me siento**, but **te sentís**. *Dormir* does the same: **duermo**, but **dormís**. In the past: **dormí** — *I slept*.' where id = '1a8b45ec-c528-5164-9c7c-bb147aad29d0' and body_md = '**Me siento mal** — *I feel sick*; **¿cómo te sentís?** — *how do you feel?* On its own, **lo siento** is *I''m sorry*. *Dormir* splits the same way: **duermo**, but **dormís** and **dormí**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For someone else it''s **se siente**: **mi abuela no se siente bien**. Where it hurts is **dolor de** — **tengo dolor de cabeza** — *I''ve got a headache*, the same as **me duele la cabeza**.' where id = '0f049b73-270c-5432-ac80-f9307754ce21' and body_md = 'For someone else it''s **se siente**: **mi abuela no se siente bien**. Where it hurts is **dolor de** — **tengo dolor de cabeza** — *I''ve got a headache*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteño thanks praise the person: **sos un genio**, **me salvaste** — *you saved me*. For a present: **¡qué detalle!** — *how thoughtful!* — or **¡te pasaste!** — *this is too much, you did an amazing job!* Said in an angry voice, the same words mean *you went too far*.' where id = '88b903ef-e0f8-5900-86f6-a2d183e36dce' and body_md = 'Porteño thanks praise the person: **sos un genio**, **me salvaste** — *you saved me*. For a present: **¡qué detalle!** — *how thoughtful!* — or **¡te pasaste!** — *you shouldn''t have!*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te debo una** — *I owe you one*. The answer is **de nada**. **No pasa nada** — *it''s fine, no worries* — is the answer to *perdón*.' where id = 'e8975dc4-db27-5349-91a4-dd07310d9224' and body_md = '**Te debo una** — *I owe you one*. The answer is **de nada**, or, more porteño, **no pasa nada**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The offer is the same pattern turned around: **¿querés que te lleve?** — *do you want me to give you a ride?*; **¿querés que traiga algo?** — the guest''s question before every *asado*. The *yo* form matches *él*: **lleve**, **traiga**, **ponga**.' where id = 'c877808b-888c-5895-a77e-cfe7de1b954b' and body_md = 'The offer is the same pattern turned around: **¿querés que te lleve?** — *want a lift?*; **¿querés que traiga algo?** — the guest''s question before every *asado*. The *yo* form matches *él*: **lleve**, **traiga**, **ponga**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Ayudar → ayudes**, **esperar → esperes**, **mandar → mandes**, **avisar → avises**. *Poner* and *traer* keep the *g* of their *yo*: **pongo → pongas**, **traigo → traiga**.' where id = '28a65e19-7a4f-501c-bed5-b872f18ca04c' and body_md = '**Ayudar → ayudes**, **esperar → esperes**, **mandar → mandes**, **avisar → avises**. *Poner* and *traer* keep the *g* of their *yo*: **pongo → pongas**, **traigo → traiga**. For *we*: **¿qué querés que hagamos?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A wish is *que* + the subjunctive: **que te vaya bien** — *good luck, hope it goes well*, also a friendly goodbye; **que la pases lindo** — *have a great time*; **que tengas buen finde**. **Pasarla** bien or mal is *to have a good or bad time*: **la pasé re mal**.' where id = '5477ef64-8dc9-564c-912e-6162a954a14d' and body_md = 'A wish is *que* + the subjunctive: **que te vaya bien** — *good luck, hope it goes well*; **que la pases lindo** — *have a great time*; **que tengas buen finde**. **Pasarla** bien or mal is *to have a good or bad time*: **la pasé re mal**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Que te vaya bien. | Good luck. |
| Que la pases lindo. | Have a great time. |
| Que tengas buen finde. | Have a good weekend. |
| Ojalá que no llueva. | I hope it doesn''t rain. |
| Ojalá salga todo bien. | I hope it all works out. |

A wish is **que** or **ojalá** + the subjunctive. After **ojalá**, *que* is optional: *ojalá que llueva* = *ojalá llueva*. *Tener → tengas, salir → salga*: the *g* of *tengo, salgo* comes along.' where id = 'c0f803fa-9e89-5bb7-a735-344a4b869d1d' and body_md = '| Que te vaya bien. | Good luck. |
| Que la pases lindo. | Have a great time. |
| Que tengas buen finde. | Have a good weekend. |
| Ojalá que no llueva. | I hope it doesn''t rain. |
| Ojalá salga todo bien. | I hope it all works out. |

A wish is **que** or **ojalá** + the subjunctive. *Tener → tengas, salir → salga*: the *g* of *tengo, salgo* comes along.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Que te mejores. | Get well soon. |
| Que te diviertas. | Have fun. |
| Que lo disfrutes. | Enjoy it. |
| Que cumplas muchos más. | I hope you have many more birthdays. |
| Ojalá que te guste. | I hope you like it. |
| Ojalá que ganemos. | I hope we win. |

The pronoun comes along into the wish: *te mejores*, *te diviertas*. For *we*, **-emos** on *-ar* verbs: *ganar* → **ganemos**. **Espero que** — *I hope* — works like *ojalá*: *espero que te guste*.' where id = '9c1177f1-7ef1-5bf5-8b98-e1a7299d3b21' and body_md = '| Que te mejores. | Get well soon. |
| Que te diviertas. | Have fun. |
| Que lo disfrutes. | Enjoy it. |
| Que cumplas muchos más. | Many happy returns. |
| Ojalá que te guste. | I hope you like it. |
| Ojalá que ganemos. | I hope we win. |

The pronoun comes along into the wish: *te mejores*, *te diviertas*. For *we*, **-emos** on *-ar* verbs: *ganar* → **ganemos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| a habit — normal verb | not yet — subjunctive |
| Cuando **vuelvo** del laburo, tomo mate. | Cuando **vuelvas**, avisame. |
| Cuando **cobro**, pago todo. | Cuando **cobre**, te invito. |
| Cuando **empiezo** a estudiar, apago el celu. | Cuando **empieces**, contame. |

**Hasta que** and **apenas** work the same way: *esperá hasta que te llame*, *apenas sepa algo, te aviso*. The open invitation: **cuando quieras**.' where id = 'c2c2634b-ae53-5d15-8f38-1640fa7e99c4' and body_md = '| a habit — normal verb | not yet — subjunctive |
| Cuando **vuelvo**, te llamo. | Cuando **vuelvas**, avisame. |
| Cuando **cobro**, pago todo. | Cuando **cobre**, te invito. |
| Cuando **empiezo**, no hablo. | Cuando **empieces**, contame. |

**Hasta que** and **apenas** work the same way: *esperá hasta que te llame*, *apenas sepa algo, te aviso*. The open invitation: **cuando quieras**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cuando quieras** — *whenever you like* — leaves an invitation open. A question with **¿cuándo?** keeps the normal verb: **¿cuándo nos vemos?** A plan with **cuando** doesn''t: **cuando nos veamos, te cuento**.' where id = 'b8dca299-9d43-5311-998f-70c610f3b72b' and body_md = '**Cuando quieras** — *whenever you like* — leaves an invitation open. The question keeps the normal verb: **¿cuándo nos vemos?** The answer doesn''t: **cuando nos veamos, te cuento**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Qué te parece?** — *what do you think?* — and the answer **me parece bien** — *sounds good* — or **me parece que no** — *I don''t think so*. **No me parece que** takes the subjunctive, like *no creo que*: *no me parece que sea caro*.' where id = '3720e015-a831-5b88-af8b-2c4948855038' and body_md = '**¿Qué te parece?** — *what do you think?* — and the answer **me parece bien**, **me parece que no**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Puede ser** — *could be* — is a common *maybe*, like **capaz**. Add *que* and the subjunctive follows: **puede ser que llueva**, **puede ser que estén cerrados**. **Es posible que** says the same, a little more carefully.' where id = '3f9a94db-3f58-5df2-a5ce-ffab9f03c71e' and body_md = '**Puede ser** — *could be* — is the porteño *maybe*. Add *que* and the subjunctive follows: **puede ser que llueva**, **puede ser que estén cerrados**. **Es posible que** says the same, a little more carefully.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| do | don''t |
| Vení. | No **vengas**. |
| Andá. | No **vayas**. |
| Decime. | No **me digas**. |
| Tocá. | No **toques**. |
| Olvidate. | No **te olvides**. |

*No* + the subjunctive (*tocar* → **toques**: the *c* turns into *qu* to keep its sound), and the pronoun moves in front: *preocupate* → **no te preocupes**. **¡No me digas!** on its own shows surprise: *no way!*' where id = '6f8ab658-e6d0-5d0b-b29e-924e5fed047b' and body_md = '| do | don''t |
| Vení. | No **vengas**. |
| Andá. | No **vayas**. |
| Decime. | No **me digas**. |
| Tocá. | No **toques**. |
| Olvidate. | No **te olvides**. |

*No* + the subjunctive, and the pronoun moves in front: *preocupate* → **no te preocupes**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**No te hagas problema** — *don''t worry about it* — is what a porteño says when you apologize. **No te olvides** — *don''t forget*: *de* + a verb (*no te olvides de llamar*); with a thing, *de* is often dropped (*no te olvides la SUBE*).' where id = '8fe89548-6879-50eb-a1b5-202ca80d4885' and body_md = '**No te hagas problema** — *don''t worry about it* — is what a porteño says when you apologize. **No te olvides** — *don''t forget*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| No **dejes** el celu en la mesa. | Don''t leave your phone on the table. |
| No **saques** la billetera. | Don''t take your wallet out. |
| No le **cuentes** a nadie. | Don''t tell anyone. |
| No **te vayas**. | Don''t go. |
| No **te pongas** nervioso. | Don''t get nervous. |
| No **seas** así. | Don''t be like that. |
Every *don''t* grows from the *yo* of the present: *dejo* → **dejes**, *cuento* → **cuentes**, *saco* → **saques** (the *c* turns *qu* to keep its sound). *Ser* and *ir* break the rule: **seas**, like *sea*, and **vayas** (*no te vayas*).' where id = '709de3f5-ef01-50d6-a9dd-5484e900d103' and body_md = '| No **dejes** el celu en la mesa. | Don''t leave your phone on the table. |
| No **saques** la billetera. | Don''t take your wallet out. |
| No le **cuentes** a nadie. | Don''t tell anyone. |
| No **te vayas**. | Don''t go. |
| No **te pongas** nervioso. | Don''t get nervous. |
| No **seas** así. | Don''t be like that. |
Every *don''t* grows from the *yo* of the present: *dejo* → **dejes**, *cuento* → **cuentes**, *saco* → **saques** (the *c* turns *qu* to keep its sound). *Ser* breaks the rule: **seas**, like *sea*. The pronoun goes in front: *me voy* → **no te vayas**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Vale la pena** — *it''s worth it*: worth the price, the trip or the wait.' where id = '3e5b7344-8608-58cc-a353-cae39fa8aefc' and body_md = '**Vale la pena** — *it''s worth it*. The highest praise a porteño gives a place.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Te aconsejo que **lleves** efectivo. | My advice: bring cash. |
| Conviene que **tomes** el subte. | Best to take the subway. |
| Es mejor que **reserves**. | Better book ahead. |
| Es importante que **uses** la SUBE. | Use your SUBE card. |
| Es mejor que **salgamos** temprano. | We''d better leave early. |

Advice with **que** takes the subjunctive. Without *que*, use the infinitive: *te conviene reservar*, *te recomiendo ir en subte*. *-ar* verbs take **e** (*llevar* → **lleves**), the rest **a** (*salgo* → **salgamos**).' where id = 'ccbc17ab-2f02-5887-84a7-3b706a5db8ec' and body_md = '| Te aconsejo que **lleves** efectivo. | My advice: bring cash. |
| Conviene que **tomes** el subte. | Best to take the subway. |
| Es mejor que **reserves**. | Better book ahead. |
| Es importante que **uses** la SUBE. | Use your SUBE card. |
| Es mejor que **salgamos** temprano. | We''d better leave early. |

Every way of giving advice takes the subjunctive. *-ar* verbs take **e** (*llevar* → **lleves**), the rest **a** (*salgo* → **salgamos**).';
update public.tips set body_md = '| ¡Qué bueno que **estés** acá! | So good you''re here! |
| Qué lástima que no **vengas**. | Shame you''re not coming. |
| Me molesta que **llegue** tarde. | It bothers me that he''s late. |

A reaction to something now or later + **que** → the subjunctive. For something that already happened, the normal past: **¡qué bueno que viniste!** **Me alegro** on its own: *I''m glad*.' where id = '9fa1891b-f569-595e-a9a2-2388d6feb5fd' and body_md = '| ¡Qué bueno que **estés** acá! | So good you''re here! |
| Qué lástima que no **vengas**. | Shame you''re not coming. |
| Me molesta que **llegue** tarde. | It bugs me he''s late. |

A reaction to something + **que** → the subjunctive. **Me alegro** on its own: *I''m glad*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me molesta que llegue tarde** — *it bothers me that he''s late*. *Molestar* works like *gustar*.' where id = '98da0042-49a1-5c74-930f-a2b3272b71a6' and body_md = '**Me molesta que llegue tarde** — *it bugs me that he''s late*. *Molestar* works like *gustar*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'After *quiero que*, *necesito que*, *no hace falta que* and *para que* (so that), the verb takes the subjunctive: **quiero que me expliques** — *I want you to explain it to me*; **no hace falta que entiendas todo** — *you don''t need to understand everything*; **mirá el video para que entiendas** — *watch the video so you understand*.' where id = 'd16cd641-7bfb-5a9b-9f9c-cea7a142d038' and body_md = 'Knowing takes the subjunctive when it''s wanted or needed: **quiero que me expliques** — *I want you to explain it to me*; **no hace falta que entiendas todo** — *you don''t need to understand everything*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te banco** — *I''m here for you*; **no lo banco** — *I can''t stand him*. One verb, opposite meanings. It also means *to wait for*: **¿me bancás acá?** — *can you wait for me here?* For things you often hear **bancarse**: *no me banco el frío* — *I can''t stand the cold*.' where id = 'e1ff50e4-f00e-575c-a7a6-7c50b9665559' and body_md = '**Te banco** — *I''ve got your back*; **no lo banco** — *I can''t stand him*. One verb, opposite meanings. It also means *to wait for*: **¿me bancás acá?** — *can you wait for me here?*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¡Qué embole!** — *how boring!* — for a rainy Sunday with nothing to do. Like all of these: friends, not job interviews.' where id = '931d857d-9b5d-5a8a-bb8f-5d48b43e1047' and body_md = '**¡Qué embole!** — *what a drag!* — for a rainy Sunday with nothing on. Like all of these: friends, not job interviews.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteño advice starts with **yo que vos** — *if I were you* — and goes straight to the conditional: **yo que vos, no le diría nada**. In everyday speech you also hear the plain present: *yo que vos, no voy*.' where id = 'ade978ac-cf4e-5fde-a04b-a5c2f59f8651' and body_md = 'Porteño advice starts with **yo que vos** — *if I were you* — and goes straight to the conditional: **yo que vos, no le diría nada**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Yo en tu lugar** — *in your shoes* — means the same as *yo que vos*, a little more serious. The advice after it is still *would*: **yo en tu lugar, hablaría con él**, **yo me quedaría**.' where id = 'f09f8f3b-acf3-5ae9-a200-3c92a0932524' and body_md = '**Yo en tu lugar** — *in your shoes* — is *yo que vos* with a straighter face. The advice after it is still *would*: **yo en tu lugar, hablaría con él**, **yo me quedaría**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'You meet the **-ra** form (*tuviera*, *pudiera*) after *si* (if) and after *ojalá* (I wish) — **ojalá pudiera**, *I wish I could* — and almost nowhere else at this level.' where id = '04f23526-26bf-5316-8fb2-a5c912c8462f' and body_md = 'You meet this form after *si* and after *ojalá* — **ojalá pudiera** — and almost nowhere else at this level.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Buenos Aires is a grid of streets cut by wide **avenidas** — Corrientes, Santa Fe, 9 de Julio. On an avenida almost every corner has a **semáforo**. Cross when it''s green: **cruzá**.' where id = '3d16b064-de20-5954-abfd-66692234787d' and body_md = 'Buenos Aires is a grid of **avenidas** — Corrientes, Santa Fe, 9 de Julio — and every corner has a **semáforo**. Cross when it''s green: **cruzá**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Leaving Buenos Aires you take **la autopista** (the fast road, with tolls), then **la ruta** (the ordinary road between towns). First you **cargás nafta** — *nafta*, never *gasolina* — and on the way you pay the **peaje**. **La General Paz** is the ring road between the Capital and the conurbano.' where id = '97e6c524-59bf-5483-b652-95a1e627cae7' and body_md = 'Leaving Buenos Aires you take **la autopista**, then **la ruta**. First you **cargás nafta** — *nafta*, never *gasolina* — and on the way you pay the **peaje**. **La General Paz** is the ring road between the Capital and the conurbano.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Your driver''s license is the **registro** — *¿tenés registro?*. Your own or rented parking space is a **cochera**; a public paid parking lot is an *estacionamiento*.' where id = '9cabde8c-14a1-59c5-afcc-463bd29cbf7f' and body_md = 'Your driver''s license is the **registro** — *¿tenés registro?*. A paid parking space or garage is a **cochera**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**No me alcanza** — *I don''t have enough* (usually money). Word for word: *it doesn''t reach for me*. **Ahorrar** is to save, **gastar** to spend: **gasté todo el sueldo**.' where id = 'b876ba73-9188-5bb8-ab20-2ee24117ccb9' and body_md = '**No me alcanza** — *it''s not enough*, *I can''t make it last*. **Ahorrar** is to save, **gastar** to spend: **gasté todo el sueldo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The question at every register. **Crédito** usually means **cuotas**, and the good ones are **sin interés**. A **caja de ahorro** (*savings account* by name) is really the everyday bank account: your pay arrives there and your debit card uses it.' where id = '719de067-63a0-5d5b-9ad3-c29affadaa38' and body_md = 'The question at every register. **Crédito** usually means **cuotas**, and the good ones are **sin interés**. Your savings sit in a **caja de ahorro**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Name your source first, then the news: **Leí en el diario que…**, **lo vi en la tele** — and **me llamó Sofi y me dijo que…**' where id = 'df56a42d-f2d8-562e-88b5-84ec61853925' and body_md = '**Leí en el diario que…**, **lo vi en la tele** — and **me llamó Sofi y me dijo que…**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Before you pass it on: **¿es cierto?** — *is it true?* — or **es mentira** — *it''s not true* (word for word, *it''s a lie*). **Lo leyó en las redes** — *she read it on social media* — is not a source.' where id = 'f448808c-e949-5196-9800-8ef7088251d6' and body_md = 'Before you pass it on: **¿es cierto?** — *is it true?* — or **es mentira** — *it''s a lie*. **Lo leyó en las redes** — *she read it on social media* — is not a source.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'One source: **mi vieja dice que…**. Several: **me contaron que…**, **me comentaron que…** — *people told me*. Porteño news travels by word of mouth and by **audio** — a WhatsApp voice message.' where id = '51b423d8-0511-58d0-8b45-1470af269ac1' and body_md = 'One source: **mi vieja dice que…**. Several: **me contaron que…**, **me comentaron que…** — *people told me*. Porteño news travels by word of mouth and by **audio**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Buena onda** is the porteño compliment for a person: easy, warm, *nice*. **Mala onda** is the opposite. **Simpático** is narrower: *friendly*, pleasant to talk to. Both stay the same for everyone: *ella es buena onda*.' where id = 'ebd8e8e5-7f3a-581d-ac16-f841077ffb75' and body_md = '**Buena onda** is the porteño compliment for a person: easy, warm, *nice*. **Mala onda** is the opposite. Both stay the same for everyone: *ella es buena onda*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Describe a group with **son** and a plural ending (**-s**, or **-es** after a consonant): **son re trabajadores**, **son medio distraídos**. A mixed group takes the masculine form.' where id = '501983de-04c6-5c67-bc94-ddd15cb1a88c' and body_md = 'Describe a group with **son** and an **-s**: **son re trabajadores**, **son medio distraídos**. A mixed group takes the *-os* form.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Two places: **quedan** — *San Isidro y Tigre quedan en zona norte*. For you: **¿te queda cerca?** — *is it close for you?*. It''s the same *queda*, with whoever it''s for in front.' where id = 'ca47c7e9-05d9-5bfa-9df1-7a8c4223003a' and body_md = 'Two places: **quedan** — *Recoleta y Belgrano quedan en zona norte*. For you: **¿te queda cerca?** — *is it close for you?*. It''s the same *queda*, with whoever it''s for in front.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Zona norte** — the suburbs north of the General Paz, like Vicente López, San Isidro and Tigre — has the money and the **árboles**; **zona sur** — the suburbs to the south, like Avellaneda, Lanús and Quilmes — is cheaper. Inside the Capital, Recoleta and Belgrano are the leafy north; Caballito, Almagro and Villa Crespo sit in the middle.' where id = 'ef2f7720-75af-506a-a7fb-1581bde273b9' and body_md = '**Zona norte** — Recoleta, Belgrano, and the suburbs past the General Paz — has the money and the **árboles**; **zona sur** — La Boca, and the conurbano to the south — is cheaper. Caballito, Almagro and Villa Crespo sit in the middle.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| what she said | what you tell |
| «¿Venís?» | Me preguntó **si venía**. |
| «Sí.» | Le contesté **que sí**. |
The question comes back with **si** — *she asked me if I was coming*; the answer with **que** — *I told her yes*. What was going on slides into the imperfect: *venís* → **venía**. If it is still true now, the present can stay: *le pregunté si viene*.' where id = '52d12bb1-c5ac-5616-9d9f-9d1183ece01e' and body_md = '| what she said | what you tell |
| «¿Venís?» | Me preguntó **si venía**. |
| «Sí.» | Le contesté **que sí**. |
The question comes back with **si** — *she asked me if I was coming*; the answer with **que** — *I told her yes*. What was going on slides into the imperfect: *venís* → **venía**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Report what someone said and the tense steps back: **viene** becomes **dijo que venía**. If it is still true now, the present can stay: **me preguntó dónde queda**.' where id = '31218369-6463-5d5f-91ce-abbcb550021c' and body_md = 'Report what someone said and the tense steps back: **viene** becomes **dijo que venía**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Dónde queda?** — *where is it?* for a place on the map. **Me queda cerca** — *it''s close to me*. Places **quedan** (or **están**); people only **están**.' where id = '4c1db3a5-2550-504b-b553-a7c7655b08aa' and body_md = '**¿Dónde queda?** — *where is it?* for a place on the map. **Me queda cerca** — *it''s close to me*. People **están**; places **quedan**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'People: **es medio vago**, **son re trabajadores**. Places: **quedan en zona norte**, **¿te queda cerca?** **Quedar** is also how clothes fit: **te queda bien**, **te queda chico**. **Te queda de paso** — *it''s on your way*.' where id = '8c3c3de9-43f2-5d5d-9b9f-e3f6f455056f' and body_md = 'People: **es medio vago**, **son re trabajadores**. Places: **quedan en zona norte**, **¿te queda cerca?**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¡Más vale!** — *of course!*; **sí o sí** — *no matter what*; **ni loco** — *no way*. Before a verb it''s *you''d better*: **más vale llevar paraguas**, **más vale que llegues temprano** (subjunctive after *que*). And when there''s too much going on: **estoy a full** — *I''m really busy*.' where id = 'c6b40c9b-6758-5732-b6d5-1a559be96347' and body_md = '**¡Más vale!** — *of course!*; **sí o sí** — *no matter what*; **ni loco** — *no way*. Before a verb it''s *you''d better*: **más vale llevar paraguas**, **más vale que llegues temprano** (subjunctive after *que*). And when there''s too much going on: **estoy a full** — *I''m flat out*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A porteño sentence breathes through its fillers: **ponele** — *let''s say*; **digamos** — *sort of*; **qué sé yo** — *I don''t know*; **bah** — *well, I mean*: *son las ocho, bah, ponele*.' where id = '6adce778-5bd3-5ead-8fc5-69d118ef84f7' and body_md = 'A porteño sentence breathes through its fillers: **ponele** — *let''s say*; **digamos** — *sort of*; **qué sé yo** — *I dunno*; **bah** — *well, I mean*: *son las ocho, bah, ponele*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Llevar** is *to take* — and also *to bring* when you''re going somewhere: **¿qué llevo al asado?** — *what should I bring?* **Yo llevo el vino** — *I''ll bring the wine*: the present does the job of *will*. To *here*, where you are, it''s **traer**: **traeme pan**.' where id = '552636d9-182b-59af-a085-35c9c07ebb3d' and body_md = '**Llevar** is *to take* — and also *to bring* when you''re going somewhere: **¿qué llevo al asado?** — *what should I bring?* **Yo llevo el vino** — *I''ll bring the wine*: the present does the job of *will*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Spanish tells accidents as if they happened *to* you: **se me cayó** — *I dropped it* (it fell, and it happened to me); **se me rompió** — *it broke on me*; **se me pasó** — *I forgot* (it slipped my mind). Nobody is to blame, which is the point.' where id = '6f7cea1b-f51c-566f-be92-462456d6f490' and body_md = 'Spanish tells accidents as if they happened *to* you: **se me cayó** — *I dropped it* (it fell on me); **se me rompió** — *it broke on me*; **se me pasó** — *I forgot* (it slipped my mind). Nobody is to blame, which is the point.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| | one thing | more than one |
| to me | **se me** quemó la comida | **se me** quemaron las tostadas |
| to you | **se te** quemó | **se te** quemaron |
| to us | **se nos** quemó | **se nos** quemaron |

The verb follows the thing: one thing **-ó**, more than one **-aron / -eron**. The middle word says who it happened to: **se me**, **se te**, **se le**, **se nos**.' where id = 'aa612ce1-aae0-5abb-ac0a-dce44906d427' and body_md = '| | one thing | more than one |
| to me | **se me** quemó la comida | **se me** cayeron las llaves |
| to you | **se te** pasó | |
| to us | **se nos** acabó el café | |

The verb follows the thing: one thing **-ó**, more than one **-aron / -eron**. The middle word says who it happened to: **se me**, **se te**, **se le**, **se nos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| same person — infinitive | someone else — subjunctive |
| Estudio **para aprender**. | Te lo explico **para que entiendas**. |
| | Te lo mando **para que lo leas**. |
| | Avisame **antes de que** llegue. |

When you tell someone to do something, **para que** is normal too: **llevá la campera para que no tengas frío**.' where id = 'c3db5128-fa8a-560f-886b-8a3374977ee4' and body_md = '| same person — infinitive | someone else — subjunctive |
| Estudio **para aprender**. | Te lo explico **para que entiendas**. |
| | Te lo mando **para que lo leas**. |
| | Avisame **antes de que** llegue. |

**Antes de que** always takes the subjunctive: it hasn''t happened yet.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Antes de que llegue** — *before he gets here* — always takes the subjunctive: it hasn''t happened yet. Same person on both sides: **antes de** + infinitive — *antes de salir*.' where id = '6448cf46-bc23-5745-bed1-552fb5525e28' and body_md = '**Antes de que llegue** — *before he gets here* — always takes the subjunctive: it hasn''t happened yet.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The subjunctive keeps the *yo* stem: *cierro* → **cierres**, *encuentro* → **encuentres**, *riego* → **riegues** (the **u** is only spelling: it keeps the *g* hard). The regular ones just swap the vowel: **entres**, **abras**.' where id = '4288460e-6410-5750-b081-94888e8c93b5' and body_md = 'The subjunctive keeps the *yo* stem: *cierro* → **cierres**, *encuentro* → **encuentres**, *riego* → **riegues**. The regular ones just swap the vowel: **entres**, **abras**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **había** | comido, llegado, salido |
| vos | **habías** | hecho, dicho, visto |
| ellos | **habían** | |
One past behind another: **Cuando llegué, ya habían comido** — *when I got there, they''d already eaten*. Pronouns go in front: **ya se había ido**, **no me habían dicho nada**. *Hecho, dicho, visto* are the irregular ones. Any participle goes with any person: **habías comido**, **había hecho**.' where id = '1ce38771-b5cc-5d17-9f00-d8a1112042e5' and body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **había** | comido, llegado, salido |
| vos | **habías** | hecho, dicho, visto |
| ellos | **habían** | |
One past behind another: **Cuando llegué, ya habían comido** — *when I got there, they''d already eaten*. Pronouns go in front: **ya se había ido**, **no me habían dicho nada**. *Hecho, dicho, visto* are the irregular ones.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **había** | probado, estado, empezado |
| vos | **habías** | terminado, escuchado |
| nosotros | **habíamos** | llamado, avisado |
| ellos | **habían** | **escrito**, hecho, dicho, visto |

Any participle goes with any person: **habíamos probado**, **habías escrito**. **Nunca había probado algo así** — never, up to a moment in the past. **Ya habíamos terminado cuando llegaste** — done before the other thing happened.' where id = '196e6740-01b2-552c-96a6-cdb74c2a7fbd' and body_md = '| yo, él, ella | **había** | probado, estado, empezado |
| vos | **habías** | terminado, escuchado |
| nosotros | **habíamos** | llamado, avisado |
| ellos | **habían** | **escrito**, hecho, dicho, visto |

**Nunca había probado algo así** — never, up to a moment in the past. **Ya habíamos terminado cuando llegaste** — done before the other thing happened.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **final** that ends in a tie goes to **penales**: the **arquero atajó** one, somebody **metió** the last, and the whole city is out in the street in the **camiseta**. A great goal is a **golazo**. **Salir campeón** is *to win the title*; **¿cómo salieron?** asks how the game ended.' where id = '0543a4d4-e086-5583-a92b-a63cb2d2b3c0' and body_md = 'A **final** that ends level goes to **penales**: the **arquero atajó** one, somebody **metió** the last, and the whole city is out in the street in the **camiseta**. A great goal is a **golazo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The other team is *they*: **ganaron**, **perdieron**, **empataron**. Yours is usually *we*, from the bar or the sofa: **¡salimos campeones!** You can still say **juegan** or **ganaron** about the players.' where id = 'aefc05cf-1bc3-5355-80ac-66c5469787aa' and body_md = 'The other team is *they*: **ganaron**, **perdieron**, **empataron**. Yours is always *we*, from the bar or the sofa: **¡salimos campeones!**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For machines, porteños say **anda** — *it works*: **no anda el wifi**, **¿anda el ascensor?**. *Funciona* means the same and is just as common.' where id = '17c1c9e2-7e28-5f37-a171-3f6f56f5e112' and body_md = 'For machines, porteños say **anda** — *it works*: **no anda el wifi**, **¿anda el ascensor?**. *Funciona* is fine, just stiffer.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'One machine **anda**, two **andan**: **no andan las pilas**. The past is irregular: **ayer anduvo bien** — *it worked fine yesterday*. **Funciona**, **funcionan** mean the same and are just as common. For *how* something works, only *funcionar*: **¿cómo funciona este control?**' where id = '5efffc1b-c968-5b0e-8d8a-6c2df5c0c497' and body_md = 'One machine **anda**, two **andan**: **no andan las pilas**. The past is irregular: **ayer anduvo bien** — *it worked fine yesterday*. **Funciona**, **funcionan** mean the same, a bit more formal — the technician''s word.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A machine that doesn''t work **no anda**: **no anda el ascensor**, **el wifi no anda**. **Funciona** means the same and is just as common. For *how* something works, only *funcionar*: **¿cómo funciona?**' where id = 'c458a9ac-cd4c-5a51-833c-9e9f01372152' and body_md = 'A machine that doesn''t work **no anda**: **no anda el ascensor**, **el wifi no anda**. **Funciona** is correct, but it''s what the manual says.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¿Me lo podés arreglar?** — *can you fix it for me?* After the **técnico** comes: **lo arregló en cinco minutos** — *he fixed it in five minutes*. If he never comes, **hacés un reclamo** — *you file a complaint* — and **nos quejamos** all summer.' where id = 'c3650361-726d-523a-93eb-fc3114f524cd' and body_md = '**¿Me lo podés arreglar?** — *can you fix it for me?* When the **técnico** has been: **lo arregló en cinco minutos**. When he hasn''t, **hacés un reclamo**, and **nos quejamos** all summer.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estoy de acuerdo** — *I agree*. Disagreeing: **no estoy de acuerdo**, or a flat **para nada** — *not at all*. In between: **depende** — *it depends*; **en parte** — *partly*.' where id = '92568dab-b1e4-5721-9f67-adeec3747987' and body_md = '**Estoy de acuerdo** — *I agree*. Disagreeing: **para nada** — *not at all*; **depende** — *it depends*; **en parte** — *partly*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Opinar** is having a view: **¿vos qué opinás?** — *what do you think?*. **Yo opino que…** sounds a bit formal: in daily speech, **para mí** starts half the sentences at a porteño table: **para mí, depende del tema**.' where id = '02a86818-3208-5fb0-9215-3197ea632302' and body_md = '**Opinar** is having a view: **¿vos qué opinás?** — *what do you think?*; **yo opino que…**. **Para mí** starts half the sentences at a porteño table: **para mí, depende del tema**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Se trae** algo. | You bring something. |
| **Se pone** la mesa. | The table gets set. |
| **Se brinda** con todos. | Everyone toasts together. |
| **Se aplaude** al asador. | Everyone applauds the grill master. |

**Se** + the *él* form: no subject, because it''s everybody. *Acá se come tarde* works the same way. On your way there, *bring* is **llevar**: **¿qué llevo?** — *what should I bring?*' where id = '79c02546-9daf-5168-b348-001f1c21de69' and body_md = '| **Se trae** algo. | You bring something. |
| **Se pone** la mesa. | The table gets set. |
| **Se brinda** con todos. | Everyone toasts together. |
| **Se aplaude** al asador. | Everyone applauds the grill master. |

**Se** + the *él* form: no subject, because it''s everybody. *Acá se come tarde* works the same way.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When the meat reaches the table, **se aplaude al asador**: *¡un aplauso para el asador!* **Se brinda** with everyone at the table. Leaving without saying goodbye to each person? Very **maleducado**.' where id = '742f77df-09f7-552b-baff-76369529b3b3' and body_md = 'At the end **se aplaude al asador**: *¡un aplauso para el asador!* **Se brinda** with everyone at the table. Leaving without saying goodbye to each person? Very **maleducado**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo que** is *what* when it means *the thing that*: **¿viste lo que pasó?**, **no sé lo que quiere**. It can start a sentence too: **lo que pasó fue raro**. A direct question keeps **qué**: *¿qué pasó?*' where id = 'c7612ab5-0ef0-58d3-b838-a200ee62dd58' and body_md = '**Lo que** is *what* in the middle of a sentence: **¿viste lo que pasó?**, **no sé lo que quiere**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¡Mirá vos!** — *oh, really?* (mild surprise) — and **no lo puedo creer** keep the story going. Porteños also say **¡no te puedo creer!** — the same thing: *I can''t believe it!* A **chusma** is someone who loves the gossip.' where id = 'eb718472-c962-5ea6-82e5-8a5d4b4100a9' and body_md = '**¡Mirá vos!** — *well, would you look at that* — and **no lo puedo creer** keep the story going. A **chusma** is someone who loves the gossip.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The second verb follows the first into the past:

| now | then |
| Quiero que **vengas**. | Quería que **vinieras**. |
| Te pido que **llames**. | Te pedí que **llamaras**. |
| Me dice que **espere**. | Me dijo que **esperara**. |

The past subjunctive is the *ellos* past with **-ra**: *vinieron* → **viniera**, *hicieron* → **hiciera**. With vos: **vinieras, hicieras, llamaras**. The *yo* and *él/ella* forms are the same: **quería que viniera** — *wanted me / him / her to come*.' where id = '74f663ec-4803-5ba8-bc3c-f12395829ac5' and body_md = 'The second verb follows the first into the past:

| now | then |
| Quiero que **vengas**. | Quería que **vinieras**. |
| Te pido que **llames**. | Te pedí que **llamaras**. |
| Me dice que **espere**. | Me dijo que **esperara**. |

The past subjunctive is the *ellos* past with **-ra**: *vinieron* → **viniera**, *hicieron* → **hiciera**. With vos: **vinieras, hicieras, llamaras**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| ellos (preterite) | yo, él, ella | vos |
| salieron | **saliera** | **salieras** |
| dijeron | **dijera** | **dijeras** |
| fueron | **fuera** | **fueras** |
| vinieron | **viniera** | **vinieras** · ellos **vinieran** |

Swap **-ron** for **-ra** and it works for every verb: *estudiar* → **estudiara, estudiaras**. **Fuera** is both *ser* and *ir*: *quería que fueras feliz* (be), *quería que fueras al asado* (go). **Mis viejos querían que estudiara una carrera** — the wish is in the past, so the second verb is too.' where id = 'dc66155e-5c8e-5a82-97d1-5269d9178812' and body_md = '| ellos (preterite) | yo, él, ella | vos |
| salieron | **saliera** | **salieras** |
| dijeron | **dijera** | **dijeras** |
| fueron | **fuera** | **fueras** |
| vinieron | **viniera** | **vinieras** · ellos **vinieran** |

Swap **-ron** for **-ra** and it works for every verb: *estudiar* → **estudiara, estudiaras**. **Mis viejos querían que estudiara una carrera** — the wish is in the past, so the second verb is too.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estricto, estricta** is *strict*. *Para salir tenía que pedir **permiso*** — *to go out I had to ask permission*. *Mi vieja **quería que volviera** temprano* — *my mom wanted me back early*.' where id = 'f4e91a43-2aa1-517a-8400-3d242229a9a1' and body_md = 'A porteño family can be **estricta**: *para salir tenía que pedir **permiso***, and my mom **quería que volviera temprano** — which never happened.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, vamos. | Aunque **llueva**, vamos. |
| Aunque **cuesta**, sigo. | Aunque **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque no **querés**, tenés que ir. | Aunque no **quieras**, tenés que ir. |

Left: it *is* raining. Right: whether or not it rains. **Igual** at the end — *anyway* — often closes it.' where id = '63fad49e-94ca-595b-9a43-f0244cd997ff' and body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, vamos. | Aunque **llueva**, vamos. |
| Aunque **cuesta**, sigo. | Aunque **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque **querés**, no podés. | Aunque no **quieras**, tenés que ir. |

Left: it *is* raining. Right: whether or not it rains. **Igual** at the end — *anyway* — often closes it.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Both start the second half: **sin embargo** — *however*, mostly in writing or formal talk — and the more spoken **así y todo** — *even so*: *hice dieta; **así y todo**, engordé*.' where id = 'a86f3f75-92ae-5f8d-ad92-17fed3596c6b' and body_md = 'Both start the second half: **sin embargo** — *however* — and the more spoken **así y todo** — *even so*: *hice dieta; **así y todo**, engordé*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Por más que** — *no matter how much* — is a stronger *aunque*: **por más que me cueste, sigo** — *however hard it is, I keep going*. A maybe takes the subjunctive, a fact doesn''t: *por más que **entreno**, engordo* — I do train; it just doesn''t show.' where id = '2df58fe2-bf8f-5caa-8c0e-83306081923b' and body_md = '**Por más que** — *no matter how much* — is *aunque* turned up: **por más que me cueste, sigo** — *however hard it is, I keep going*. A maybe takes the subjunctive, a fact doesn''t: *por más que **entreno**, engordo* — I do train; it just doesn''t show.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, entreno. | Aunque **llueva**, entreno igual. |
| Por más que me **cuesta**, sigo. | Por más que me **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque no **tengo** ganas, voy. | Aunque no **tenga** ganas, voy igual. |

**Por más que** is a stronger *aunque*. **Aunque sea** — *even just*: *aunque sea un rato*. **Sin embargo, así y todo** start the other half.' where id = '5d9cf103-d9b8-5f59-afa3-d19b7d920777' and body_md = '| a fact — normal verb | a maybe — subjunctive |
| Aunque **llueve**, entreno. | Aunque **llueva**, entreno igual. |
| Por más que me **cuesta**, sigo. | Por más que me **cueste**, sigo. |
| Aunque no **tengo** ganas, voy. | Aunque no **tenga** ganas, voy igual. |

**Por más que** is *aunque* turned up. **Aunque sea** — *even just*: *aunque sea un rato*. **Sin embargo, así y todo** start the other half.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Llevo dos años **viviendo** acá. | I''ve been living here for two years. |
| Hace dos años que **vivo** acá. | (the same) |
| **Sigo** laburando ahí. | I still work there. |
| **Dejé de** fumar. | I quit smoking. |
| **Volvió a** llamar. | He called again. |
English *have been …ing* is the present in Spanish. With a past verb, **hace … que** means *ago*: *hace dos años que dejé de fumar* — *I quit two years ago*. **Llevar** + time + *-ando, -iendo* — or just a place: **lleva un año acá**. **Llevo / sigo sin** + infinitive is *haven''t … / still not*: *llevo seis meses sin fumar*.' where id = '75167017-65a6-5a49-9a02-adfb338b796b' and body_md = '| Llevo dos años **viviendo** acá. | I''ve been living here for two years. |
| Hace dos años que **vivo** acá. | (the same) |
| **Sigo** laburando ahí. | I still work there. |
| **Dejé de** fumar. | I quit smoking. |
| **Volvió a** llamar. | He called again. |
English *have been …ing* is the present in Spanish. **Llevar** + time + *-ando, -iendo* — or just a place: **lleva un año acá**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| ¿**Hace cuánto** que estudiás? | How long have you been studying? |
| **Llevo** un año **aprendiendo**. | I''ve been learning for a year. |
| Mis amigos **llevan** meses **buscando** laburo. | My friends have been looking for work for months. |
| **Seguimos** practicando. / **Siguen** tratando. | We''re still practicing. / They keep trying. |
| **Dejaron de** venir. | They stopped coming. |
| **Volví a** estudiar. | I went back to studying. |
**Desde que** llegué — *since I arrived* — counts from a moment instead.' where id = '58f46de1-33f5-5cc3-afe9-3806d0902cee' and body_md = '| ¿**Hace cuánto** que estudiás? | How long have you been studying? |
| **Llevo** un año **aprendiendo**. | I''ve been learning for a year. |
| Mis amigos **llevan** meses **buscando** laburo. | My friends have been job-hunting for months. |
| **Seguimos** practicando. / **Siguen** tratando. | We''re still practicing. / They keep trying. |
| **Dejaron de** venir. | They stopped coming. |
| **Volví a** estudiar. | I went back to studying. |
**Desde que** llegué — *since I arrived* — counts from a moment instead.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**¡Buen provecho!** — *enjoy!* — is polite when you serve food or walk in on people eating; at home, people often just start. And when the host says **sírvanse** — *help yourselves* — everybody starts right away.' where id = '1a5ebe3a-b4e7-546a-b4ed-cb9dba0344f7' and body_md = 'Before the first bite: **¡buen provecho!** — *enjoy!* And when the host says **sírvanse** — *help yourselves* — nobody waits to be asked twice.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| one person (vos) | more than one (ustedes) |
| probá | **prueben** |
| agarrá | **agarren** |
| tomá | **tomen** |
| no te olvides | **no se olviden** |

Also **coman**, **hagan** lugar, **vayan**, **dejen**. **Vayan** + *-ando/-iendo* is *go ahead and start*: **vayan comiendo** — *start eating*. -ar verbs **-en**, the rest **-an**. The stem is the *yo* stem: *pruebo* → **prueben**, *hago* → **hagan**, *vengo* → **vengan**. The pronoun sticks on the end — **sírvanse, apúrense** — and after *no* it goes in front: **no se olviden**.' where id = 'a5ed425f-69c3-5b5d-816e-3fc1878a9d27' and body_md = '| one person (vos) | more than one (ustedes) |
| probá | **prueben** |
| agarrá | **agarren** |
| tomá | **tomen** |
| no te olvides | **no se olviden** |

Also **coman**, **hagan** lugar, **vayan**, **dejen**. -ar verbs **-en**, the rest **-an**. The pronoun sticks on the end — **sírvanse, apúrense** — and after *no* it goes in front: **no se olviden**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| yo | **me hice** el distraído | I pretended not to notice |
| vos | **te hacés** el sordo | you act like you can''t hear |
| él, ella | **se hace** el canchero | he acts all cool |
| | como si no **pasara** nada | as if nothing were happening |
| | como si no me **viera** | as if he didn''t see me |

**No te hagas el gil** — *don''t play dumb*. A woman says **la**: *me hice **la** simpática*, *se hace **la** sorda*. After **como si** and **ni que**, always the *-ra* form: *¡ni que **fueras** mi viejo!* But **hace como que** takes a normal verb: *hace como que no le importa*.' where id = '3e245af1-6d97-5dae-8ef1-7ab6426eb575' and body_md = '| yo | **me hice** el distraído | I pretended not to notice |
| vos | **te hacés** el sordo | you act like you can''t hear |
| él, ella | **se hace** el canchero | he acts all cool |
| | como si no **pasara** nada | as if nothing were happening |
| | como si no me **viera** | as if he didn''t see me |

**No te hagas el gil** — *don''t play dumb*. After **como si** and **ni que**, always the *-ra* form: *¡ni que **fueras** mi viejo!*';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **caradura** has no shame: never pays, asks for too much, lies with a straight face. **¡Qué caradura!** — *you''ve got some nerve!* Between friends it''s often a joke.' where id = '8e0594ac-1009-51d2-b934-d91eaaa7f29c' and body_md = 'Someone who does it with a straight face is a **caradura** — *shameless, cheeky*: **¡qué caradura!** Between friends it''s almost a compliment.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For more than one person: **pasen** — *come in*; **vengan** — *come*; **siéntense** — *sit down*; **pónganse cómodos** — *make yourselves comfortable*; **no se preocupen** — *don''t worry*.' where id = '02ccd3ab-67b7-5899-aaa7-64f6847cb270' and body_md = 'For more than one person: **pasen**, **vengan**, **siéntense**, **no se preocupen**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For a group: **coman**, **prueben**, **sírvanse**, **no se olviden**. The *no* doesn''t change the verb, only where the pronoun goes: **siéntense** → **no se sienten**; **sírvanse** → **no se sirvan**.' where id = 'd5688bae-b7ba-57fc-b691-b14418254954' and body_md = 'For a group: **coman**, **prueben**, **sírvanse**, **no se olviden**. The *no* doesn''t change the verb, only where the pronoun goes.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Como si** takes the past subjunctive: *como si supiera*. **El que, la que** — *the one that*: *la que prefieras*. **Aunque** + normal verb — *even though* (a fact): *aunque estoy cansada*; + subjunctive — *even if*: *aunque llueva*.' where id = 'a8ab9b46-086f-55ce-98d9-cbf02a2d003b' and body_md = '**Como si** takes the past subjunctive: *como si supiera*. **El que, la que** — *the one that*: *la que prefieras*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'When nobody''s to blame: **¡qué mala suerte!** And at Ezeiza, the international airport, the board says what every porteño expects: the flight is **demorado** — *delayed*.' where id = 'd338d3db-f4ad-55cc-8eab-5ce4e8d0c03c' and body_md = 'When nobody''s to blame: **¡qué mala suerte!** And at Ezeiza the board says what every porteño expects: the flight is **demorado** — *delayed*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Por un lado… por otro lado** weighs two sides. **En cambio** — *but, on the other hand* — sets two people or things against each other: *yo laburo, en cambio él no*.' where id = '4cb250cf-f227-501f-aefc-fb7775e2e1ca' and body_md = '**Por un lado… por otro lado** weighs two sides. **En cambio** — *whereas* — sets two people or things against each other: *yo laburo, en cambio él no*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**De hecho** — *in fact* — backs up what you just said: *no es caro; de hecho, es barato*. **En realidad** — *actually* — corrects it: *en realidad no es tan caro*. **Por eso** — *that''s why*: *está cerca, por eso me gusta*.' where id = 'b2d04c3b-a80f-5173-ba94-693c40ae1e39' and body_md = '**De hecho** — *in fact* — backs up what you just said. **En realidad** — *actually* — corrects it: *en realidad no es tan caro*. **Por eso** — *that''s why*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For almost anything official you first **sacás turno** — you book an appointment online — and you bring the **DNI**, the national ID card, without which nothing happens. As a foreigner, you use your passport until you get your own DNI.' where id = '96bfd871-c811-5edf-8fe3-6f07c3c37007' and body_md = 'For almost anything official you first **sacás turno** — you book an appointment online — and you bring the **DNI**, the national ID card, without which nothing happens.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For paperwork, **demorar** is how long something takes: **¿cuánto demora la residencia?** In everyday talk porteños mostly say **tardar**: *el colectivo tarda*. The honest answer is *depende*. You **presentás** the papers, and when they finally **atienden** you, it''s over in five minutes.' where id = '0a7f761b-d9c7-516c-b579-5874def00152' and body_md = 'Porteños say **demorar** for how long something takes: **¿cuánto demora la residencia?** The honest answer is *depende*. You **presentás** the papers, and when they finally **atienden** you, it''s over in five minutes.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| Me **pone nervioso** que llegue tarde. | It makes me nervous that he''s late. |
| Me **enoja** que me **mienta**. | It makes me angry that he lies to me. |
| Me **alegra** que vengas. | I''m glad you''re coming. |
| Me da bronca que **cancele**. | It makes me mad that he cancels. |

Feeling first, then **que** + subjunctive. If it''s you doing it, no *que*: *me enoja **llegar** tarde*.' where id = '71b73b1e-ae85-5fc6-9381-abc5a40d2806' and body_md = '| Me **pone nervioso** que llegue tarde. | It drives me crazy that he''s late. |
| Me **enoja** que me **mienta**. | It makes me angry that he lies to me. |
| Me **alegra** que vengas. | I''m glad you''re coming. |
| Me da bronca que **cancele**. | It makes me mad that he cancels. |

Feeling first, then **que** + subjunctive. If it''s you doing it, no *que*: *me enoja **llegar** tarde*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The porteño complaint of the WhatsApp age: **me clavó el visto** — *he read my message and didn''t answer*. And the friend who forgets everything is **re colgado**.' where id = 'b1156beb-77bd-582d-8612-8edf301649c5' and body_md = 'The porteño complaint of the WhatsApp age: **me clavó el visto** — *he left me on read*. And the friend who forgets everything is **re colgado**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Deberías** descansar. | You should rest. |
| **Debería** llamarla. | I should call her. |
| **Estaría bueno** juntarnos. | It''d be nice to get together. |
| **Habría que** avisarle. | We ought to let him know. |

All four can take an infinitive. **Estaría bueno** also takes **que** + subjunctive: *estaría bueno que vengas*. *Tenés que* is stronger — *you have to*; *deberías* is advice.' where id = '4f42bca0-b0c9-54dd-894d-af1e0ddee783' and body_md = '| **Deberías** descansar. | You should rest. |
| **Debería** llamarla. | I should call her. |
| **Estaría bueno** juntarnos. | It''d be nice to get together. |
| **Habría que** avisarle. | We ought to let him know. |

All four take an infinitive. *Tenés que* is an order; *deberías* is advice.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To stress a promise, porteños say **me aseguró que…** — *he assured me* — or **me juró que…** — *he swore*. Then comes the **excusa** (*excuse*), and you learn not to **confiar en** (*trust*) the **mentiroso** (*liar*).' where id = '5aaa801b-ae20-5109-886b-c9cff7a1d334' and body_md = 'Porteños rarely just *say* a promise: **me aseguró que**, **me juró que**. Then comes the **excusa** — and you learn not to **confiar** in the **mentiroso**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| one thing | more than one |
| **Se vende** auto. | **Se venden** bicis. |
| **Se alquila** depto. | **Se alquilan** deptos. |
| **Se necesita** mozo. | **Se necesitan** mozos. |

**Se** + the *él* form, or the *ellos* form for plurals. Nobody is named: it''s what''s being sold, rented, needed.' where id = 'a13868ae-2900-572c-98a0-bf4c01691f94' and body_md = '| one thing | more than one |
| **Se vende** auto. | **Se venden** bicis. |
| **Se alquila** depto. | |
| **Se necesita** mozo. | |

**Se** + the *él* form, or the *ellos* form for plurals. Nobody is named: it''s what''s being sold, rented, needed.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The building speaks the same way: **no se permiten mascotas**, **se prohíbe hacer ruido después de las diez**. That''s written language: out loud people say **se puede** / **no se puede**. On the shop door: **horario de atención** — and outside those hours the **local** is **cerrado**.' where id = 'af4c1031-7c9c-5fb0-8d8b-5b57bb841bd4' and body_md = 'The building speaks the same way: **no se permiten mascotas**, **se prohíbe hacer ruido después de las diez**. On the shop door: **horario de atención** — and the **local** is often **cerrado** at lunchtime.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| one thing | more than one |
| **Se busca** perro. | **Se aceptan** tarjetas. |
| **Se permite** fumar en la terraza. | No **se permiten** mascotas. |
| **Se prohíbe** hacer ruido. | **Se hacen** envíos. |

The verb agrees with the thing: one → *se busca*, several → *se arreglan bicis*. Most real signs just say **Prohibido fumar**; **se prohíbe** is the formal version.' where id = 'e9b64ef7-a37a-5cfb-ae67-7f9141722279' and body_md = '| one thing | more than one |
| **Se busca** perro. | **Se aceptan** tarjetas. |
| **Se permite** fumar en la terraza. | No **se permiten** mascotas. |
| **Se prohíbe** hacer ruido. | **Se hacen** envíos. |

The verb agrees with the thing: one → *se busca*, several → *se arreglan bicis*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Reported promises go into *would*: **dijo que vendría**, **me prometiste que me llamarías**. Out loud, porteños more often say **dijo que iba a venir**; *vendría* is correct but more careful.' where id = '7bc7cb49-45ee-5195-b8b6-8be5a6f0a0a3' and body_md = 'Reported promises go into *would*: **dijo que vendría**, **me prometiste que me llamarías**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Con tal de que me lo devuelvas** — *as long as you give it back* — and **salvo que lo necesite** — *unless I need it* — take the subjunctive. On the door: **se aceptan tarjetas**, **se hacen envíos**.' where id = '2d79110f-684e-5df1-978a-1dbfe56b6cc3' and body_md = '**Con tal de que me lo devuelvas** and **salvo que lo necesite** take the subjunctive. On the door: **se aceptan tarjetas**, **se hacen envíos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'What he swore he''d do, told later: **dijo que pasaría**, **me aseguró que me lo devolvería**. Two have a changed stem: *poner* → **pondría**, *venir* → **vendría**.' where id = 'bf2dc98a-75d6-56a8-a981-915fd847826c' and body_md = 'What he swore he''d do, told later: **dijo que pasaría**, **me aseguró que me lo devolvería**. **Pondría** keeps its odd stem.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Prices **suben** — or **aumentan**, same thing — and, now and then, **bajan**. **¿Cuánto te cobraron?** — *how much did they charge you?* A **precio** is a price; *está a buen precio* — *it''s a good price*.' where id = '8af67e04-9d96-5ada-98ea-78bbea30080c' and body_md = 'Prices **suben** and, now and then, **bajan**. **¿Cuánto te cobraron?** — *how much did they charge you?* A **precio** is a price; *está a buen precio* — *it''s a good price*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Bills come in plural, and so do the verbs: **aumentaron la luz y el gas**, **aumentan las tarifas**. The plural can also be a nameless *they*: **me aumentaron el alquiler** — *they raised my rent*. Prices that **bajaron**? Nobody remembers. Porteños keep count: *el **boleto** aumentó tres veces este año*.' where id = 'da398a9c-7a73-5939-919b-d39bf8d6858f' and body_md = 'Bills come in plural, and so do the verbs: **aumentaron la luz y el gas**, **aumentan las tarifas**. Prices that **bajaron**? Nobody remembers. Porteños keep count: *el **boleto** aumentó tres veces este año*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Ando buscando** laburo. | I''m looking around for work. |
| **Voy conociendo** gente. | I''m getting to know people. |
| **Estamos por** arrancar. | We''re about to start. |
| Estoy **a punto de** terminar. | I''m just about to finish. |

**Ando** + *-ando* is these days, on and off, not this very second; **voy** + *-ando* happens bit by bit.' where id = 'ec66006c-2d54-5e6c-9c71-4c5cc4a097d1' and body_md = '| **Ando buscando** laburo. | I''m looking around for work. |
| **Voy conociendo** gente. | I''m getting to know people. |
| **Estamos por** arrancar. | We''re about to start. |
| Estoy **a punto de** terminar. | I''m just about to finish. |

**Andar** + gerund is looser than *estar*; **ir** + gerund grows bit by bit.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'With **ir**, it grows bit by bit: **voy conociendo gente**, **el bondi se va llenando**, **me voy acostumbrando al ritmo**. It''s the verb of settling in. Careful: in **andá llenando la pava**, *andá* is the command of *ir* (go): *start filling the kettle*.' where id = 'bbdfc70e-908b-560e-840e-ba134a2e4dc1' and body_md = 'With **ir**, it grows bit by bit: **voy conociendo gente**, **el bondi se va llenando**, **me voy acostumbrando al ritmo**. It''s the verb of settling in.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estamos por arrancar** — *we''re about to start*. **A punto de** means the same, only even sooner: **estoy a punto de terminar**.' where id = '5bbac630-a58e-519b-b308-312edbba56a6' and body_md = '**Estamos por arrancar** — *we''re about to start*. **A punto de** is the same, a hair closer: **estoy a punto de terminar**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The other end: **no lo aguanto** — *I can''t stand him*; **es insoportable**; **es re falso**. And the good end: **nos hicimos amigos** — *we became friends*. And **hay química** — *there''s chemistry* — is mostly said about a couple.' where id = 'd8cbc098-8879-5b9f-bf4d-675b87f2a096' and body_md = 'The other end: **no lo aguanto** — *I can''t stand him*; **es insoportable**; **es re falso**. And the good end: **nos hicimos amigos** — *we became friends* — because **hay química**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Ni a palos** — *no way, not a chance*. And for a shrug: **dale que va** — *good enough, let''s go*. When something''s awful: **está de terror**.' where id = 'e2b47401-0cfc-5d9f-9194-4ecbb72de555' and body_md = '**Ni a palos** — *not in a million years*. The opposite shrug: **dale que va** — *good enough, let''s go*. When something''s awful: **está de terror**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The other persons follow: **nos pidió que llegáramos temprano** — *she asked us to get there early*; **les dijo que trajeran algo** — *he told them to bring something*. **Encargar** is to give someone an errand: **me encargó que le llevara el pan** — *she asked me to bring her the bread*.' where id = '2bf931e1-9673-5e55-aa7e-198aafe4ff0d' and body_md = 'The other persons follow: **nos pidió que llegáramos temprano** — *she asked us to get there early*; **les dijo que trajeran algo** — *he told them to bring something*. **Me encargó que le llevara** is the errand version: *she asked me to take her…*';
update public.tips set body_md = '**A ver si** is *let''s see if* — and, just as often, a hope: **a ver si nos juntamos** — *we should get together sometime*. To find something out, porteños **averiguan**. After **dudo que**, the verb goes in the subjunctive: **dudo que venga** — *I doubt he''ll come*.' where id = 'ec1122a7-6b09-5324-b5c9-305542cf61e1' and body_md = '**A ver si** is *let''s see if* — and, just as often, a hope: **a ver si nos juntamos** — *we should get together sometime*. To find something out, porteños **averiguan**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| the question | asking or telling it |
| «¿Tienen stock?» | **Preguntale si** tienen stock. |
| «¿Abren el feriado?» | **Me fijo si** abren el feriado. |
| «¿Tenés turno?» | **Me preguntaron si** tenía turno. |
| «¿Está disponible?» | No sé **si** está disponible. |

**Si** is *whether*, and the verb after it is the normal one. Told later, it moves into the past: *tenés* → *tenía*. If it is still true now, the present is fine too: *me preguntaron si soy argentino*.' where id = 'b1075fbe-1362-54f2-9d90-7a83352ec36b' and body_md = '| the question | asking or telling it |
| «¿Tienen stock?» | **Preguntale si** tienen stock. |
| «¿Abren el feriado?» | **Me fijo si** abren el feriado. |
| «¿Tenés turno?» | **Me preguntaron si** tenía turno. |
| «¿Está disponible?» | No sé **si** está disponible. |

**Si** is *whether*, and the verb after it is the normal one. Told later, it moves into the past: *tenés* → *tenía*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteños say **vos** to almost everyone: the shop owner, a doctor, an old man on the bus. You may still hear **usted** sometimes, but **vos** is always fine for you. The politeness lives in the words around it: **disculpá que te moleste**, **perdón por la molestia**, **muy amable**.' where id = 'dda7b964-bb56-5e48-bc13-d19abd0fc766' and body_md = 'Porteños say **vos** to everyone: the shop owner, a doctor, an old man on the bus. The politeness lives in the words around it: **disculpá que te moleste**, **perdón por la molestia**, **muy amable**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The old neighbor is **don José** or **doña Rosa** — first name, with respect. A **persona mayor**, a **jubilado**, still gets **vos**, plus a **cómo no** (*of course*) and a **con permiso** when you need to get past.' where id = '0da84ce9-08d5-56d5-bf04-81b8a54b1746' and body_md = 'The old neighbor is **don José** or **doña Rosa** — first name, with respect. A **persona mayor**, a **jubilado**, still gets **vos**, plus a **cómo no** (*of course*) and a **con permiso** as you squeeze past.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'More verbs that take a **la** pointing at nothing: **me la juego** — *I''ll go for it*; **la pifié** — *I blew it*; **la rompe** — *she''s amazing at it*; **se la agarró conmigo** — *he took it out on me* (he got angry at me, though it wasn''t my fault). **Me las tomo** — *I''m out of here*.' where id = '22bb24f8-8694-59d9-9551-1eae8071c382' and body_md = 'More verbs that take a **la** pointing at nothing: **me la juego** — *I''ll go for it*; **la pifié** — *I blew it*; **la rompe** — *she nails it, she kills it*; **se la agarró conmigo** — *he took it out on me*. **Me las tomo** — *I''m out of here*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Resulta que** — *it turns out*; **encima** — *on top of that*; **total** — *after all, anyway* (it doesn''t matter): **vamos a pie, total es cerca**.' where id = 'd1e06ff5-4048-5e50-818b-97cd025a4f74' and body_md = '**Resulta que** turns the story, **encima** makes it worse, **total** shrugs.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Se la cree** — *he''s arrogant*; **me la banco** — *I can handle it*; **me las arreglo** — *I manage*; **la tenés clara** — *you know your stuff*. The *la* points at nothing.' where id = 'f8f1dd38-6b20-5a33-9fa8-3f6dc3e87775' and body_md = '**Se la cree**, **me la banco**, **me las arreglo**, **la tenés clara** — a *la* that points at nothing.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me la jugué** — *I took the risk*; **la pifié** — *I messed up*; **la rompe** — *he''s amazing*; **te las arreglás** — *you manage*. The same *la* that points at nothing.' where id = '83235091-134e-5789-949b-4252689bf7a7' and body_md = '**Me la jugué**, **la pifié**, **la rompe**, **te las arreglás** — the *la* again, doing nothing and everything.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Acabo de** llegar. | I just got here. |
| **Suelo** almorzar tarde. | I usually have lunch late. |
| **Volví a** perder las llaves. | I lost my keys again. |

All three take an infinitive. **Soler** has a past too, **solía** — *solía almorzar tarde* — but *antes almorzaba tarde* says the same.' where id = '19d601d6-de61-5a96-92de-c8ebe98b3a8f' and body_md = '| **Acabo de** llegar. | I just got here. |
| **Suelo** almorzar tarde. | I usually have lunch late. |
| **Volví a** perder las llaves. | I lost my keys again. |

All three take an infinitive. **Soler** has no past you''ll need: *antes almorzaba tarde* does the job.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Acabo de** + infinitive is *I just did it*: **acabo de llegar**, **acaba de salir**. **Volví a** is *I did it again*: **volví a perder las llaves**. Or just **de nuevo** or **otra vez** — *again*.' where id = '043bf160-0648-51c6-bec2-2b7afbcb4c4a' and body_md = '**Acabo de** + infinitive is *I just did it*: **acabo de llegar**, **acaba de salir**. **Volví a** is *I did it again*: **volví a perder las llaves**. Or just **de nuevo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Dejar de** + infinitive is *to stop, to quit*: **dejé de fumar**, **¿dejaste de ir al gimnasio?**, **¡dejá de quejarte!** Its opposite is **volver a**: **volvió a fumar** — *he started smoking again*. **Ponerse a** is *to start doing*: **me puse a estudiar** — *I started studying*.' where id = '1ff21937-4c97-54d5-9f50-7a6407f83159' and body_md = '**Dejar de** + infinitive is *to stop, to quit*: **dejé de fumar**, **¿dejaste de ir al gimnasio?**, **¡dejá de quejarte!** Its opposite is **volver a** — **volvió a fumar** — or **ponerse a**, *to get down to it*: **me puse a estudiar**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Acabamos de** llegar. | We just got here. |
| Los porteños **suelen** cenar tarde. | Porteños usually have dinner late. |
| **Volvió a** fumar. | He started smoking again. |
| **Dejé de** fumar. | I quit smoking. |
| **Me puse a** estudiar. | I started studying. |

All five take an infinitive straight after: *acabar de, soler, volver a, dejar de, ponerse a*.' where id = '2ec6d8dd-06cf-5988-b62d-9b3c19590195' and body_md = '| **Acabamos de** llegar. | We just got here. |
| Los porteños **suelen** cenar tarde. | Porteños usually have dinner late. |
| **Volvió a** fumar. | He started smoking again. |
| **Dejé de** fumar. | I quit smoking. |
| **Me puse a** estudiar. | I got down to studying. |

All five take an infinitive straight after: *acabar de, soler, volver a, dejar de, ponerse a*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Crecer** is *to grow* — a city, a kid, a tree: **el barrio creció**, **crecí en Rosario** — *I grew up in Rosario*. A building is an **edificio**: **hay cada vez más edificios**.' where id = '3b867a4a-8a39-52fc-bdb4-73a4c0c46453' and body_md = '**Crecer** is *to grow* — a city, a kid, a tree: **el barrio creció**, **crecí en Rosario** — *I grew up in Rosario*. The new towers are **edificios**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cada vez peor** and **cada vez mejor** — *worse and worse, better and better*. What''s in is **de moda**; what''s gone **desapareció**: **desaparecieron los almacenes** — *the corner shops disappeared*, and where the old house stood there''s a **torre** — *a high-rise*. Ya no es **lo mismo** — *it''s not the same anymore*.' where id = '540d8ca7-657a-5701-bb91-0246d4d77115' and body_md = '**Cada vez peor** and **cada vez mejor** — *worse and worse, better and better*. What''s in is **de moda**; what''s gone **desapareció**: **desaparecieron los almacenes**, and where the old house stood there''s a **torre**. Ya no es **lo mismo**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me quejo** — *I complain*; **reniego** is the Argentine *I struggle with it, I grumble*: **reniego todos los días con el banco**. Someone who''s **agotado** is *exhausted*; the **estrés** is why. And the traffic? **Un caos**.' where id = '6f45a3bc-6d31-5a43-8fae-bde8329e1e96' and body_md = '**Me quejo** — *I complain*; **reniego** is the Argentine *I struggle with it, I grumble*: **reniego todos los días con el banco**. Someone who''s **agotado** is *wiped out*; the **estrés** is why. And the traffic? **Un caos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Y bueno** is the porteño shrug — *oh well, what can you do*: **y bueno, así es**. **Ah, me olvidaba** — *oh, I forgot to say* — adds the best part at the end. A story can be **larga** — *long* — or **corta** — *short*.' where id = 'c94d2e69-9d48-539a-a1af-33cdcb771363' and body_md = '**Y bueno** is the porteño shrug — *oh well, what can you do*: **y bueno, así es**. **Ah, me olvidaba** — *oh, I forgot to say* — adds the best part at the end. A story can be **larga** or **corta**; this one never is.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te la hago corta** — *to keep it short* — is usually followed by a long story. **La cuestión es que** — *the point is* — gets to what matters, like **el tema es que**; **en fin** closes it.' where id = '534e2bd7-f308-543e-af35-642336a8e744' and body_md = '**Te la hago corta** — *long story short* — is usually followed by a long story. **La cuestión es que** — *the thing is* — brings it back on track; **en fin** closes it.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Funcionar** is *to work* for things: **el subte no funciona**, **los semáforos no funcionan**. In everyday talk porteños also say **andar**: *el ascensor no anda*. People *trabajan* or *laburan*.' where id = '6ce81526-2ff0-5977-9bbf-fd1e8d406e0b' and body_md = '**Funcionar** is *to work* for things: **el subte no funciona**, **los semáforos no funcionan**. For people, it''s still *laburar*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The news likes the passive: **fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective: **el puente fue construido**, **la estación fue inaugurada**; more than one: **fueron detenidos** — *they were arrested*. In conversation porteños turn it around: *construyeron el puente*, *los detuvieron*. For the future the news says **será inaugurada** — *will be opened*; people say *la van a inaugurar*.' where id = '5f88a88d-8066-58cb-99c8-edeb9d5d9112' and body_md = 'The news likes the passive: **fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective: **el puente fue construido**, **la estación fue inaugurada**; more than one: **fueron detenidos** — *they were arrested*. In conversation porteños turn it around: *construyeron el puente*, *los detuvieron*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Both parts agree with what it''s about — **fue**/**fueron** for one or many, and the ending **-o/-a/-os/-as**: **el boliche fue clausurado**, **la obra fue clausurada**, **los vecinos fueron rescatados**, **las vecinas fueron rescatadas**. Whoever did it comes after **por**: *por los bomberos*. **Fue clausurado** is the event — *it got closed down*; **está clausurado** is the result — *it is closed now*.' where id = '22681126-952e-59e5-97e2-12d780e48738' and body_md = 'The headline verb agrees with what it''s about: **el boliche fue clausurado**, **la obra fue clausurada**, **los vecinos fueron rescatados**, **las vecinas fueron rescatadas**. Whoever did it comes after **por**: *por los bomberos*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| El puente **fue construido** hace un siglo. | was built |
| La estación **fue inaugurada** ayer. | was opened |
| Los chorros **fueron detenidos**. | were arrested |

**Fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective. In conversation: *construyeron el puente*. **Detenidos** is also a noun: *hay dos detenidos* — *two people were arrested*.' where id = 'de7cd7bc-7f0d-588c-bc69-c90f2dc4f004' and body_md = '| El puente **fue construido** hace un siglo. | was built |
| La estación **fue inaugurada** ayer. | was opened |
| Los chorros **fueron detenidos**. | were arrested |

**Fue** + participle, and the participle agrees like an adjective. In conversation: *construyeron el puente*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In Argentina voting is **obligatorio** from 18 to 70 (optional at 16–17 and after 70). **¿A quién votaste?** is a real question, though many answer **eso no se pregunta**. **Votar a** someone: *voté a la misma candidata*. **Votar por** works too: *¿por quién votás?*' where id = '67c1e923-9983-5e50-a6ce-52ff85a6eb09' and body_md = 'In Argentina voting is **obligatorio**. **¿A quién votaste?** is a real question, though many answer **eso no se pregunta**. **Votar a** someone: *voté a la misma candidata*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The **cuarto oscuro** — *the dark room* — is where you vote alone. In national elections since 2025 you get one **boleta** at your mesa, mark it behind a screen and put it in the **urna**. People still say cuarto oscuro, and some provinces keep the old party ballots. The **voto** is secret. If nobody wins outright, there''s a **balotaje** — *a runoff*. Missed it? You have to **justificar** why.' where id = '60436255-a5f1-5601-8f69-39f8dd6f913a' and body_md = 'The booth is the **cuarto oscuro** — *the dark room* — where you pick your **boleta** and drop it in the **urna**. The **voto** is secret. If nobody wins outright, there''s a **balotaje** — *a runoff*. Missed it? You have to **justificar** why.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Election day is a Sunday, and everyone asks **¿dónde votás?** You check the **padrón** — *the voter roll* — for your school and your **mesa** — *your voting table*. **Votamos** in the school around the corner; **mi abuela votó a las ocho**, first in line.' where id = '2a3a2462-0e4e-58df-9bc1-fcf6e909f66e' and body_md = 'Election day is a Sunday, and everyone asks **¿dónde votás?** You check the **padrón** — *the voter roll* — for your school and your **mesa**. **Votamos** in the school around the corner; **mi abuela votó a las ocho**, first in line.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Paro docente**, **suspendieron las clases**, **hubo desvíos** — and the city **a pie**.' where id = 'a7707333-9bed-5180-8835-8a8805c92044' and body_md = '**Paro docente**, **suspendieron el servicio**, **hubo desvíos** — and the city **a pie**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me estafaron** — *I got scammed* : nobody grabs anything, they trick you. A fake call from the bank, a **billete trucho**, or the **cuento del tío**: a caller pretends to be a relative or an official and asks for money. First thing: **bloqueá la tarjeta**. Then the denuncia; if you''re lucky, the street **cámaras** recorded it.' where id = '68bbdfb3-c560-5eab-a9a4-e53a956ef37d' and body_md = '**Me estafaron** — *I got scammed* — is quieter: a call from a fake bank, a **billete trucho**, the **cuento del tío** — *the old con* — on your grandmother. First thing: **bloqueá la tarjeta**. Then the denuncia, with the **cámaras** of the block if you''re lucky.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The confession that comes with it: **me descuidé** — *I wasn''t careful*. Porteños answer **¡qué garrón!**' where id = 'a9d44d65-c0ea-523c-a2ec-38cdabf80bdc' and body_md = 'The confession that comes with it: **me descuidé** — *I let my guard down*. Porteños answer **¡qué garrón!**';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **me** robaron | they robbed me |
| **te** robaron | they robbed you |
| **le** robaron a mi vieja | they robbed my mom |
| **nos** robaron la bici | they stole our bike |
| **me** afanaron, **me** estafaron | they stole it, they scammed me |
The verb stays *robaron*; the pronoun in front says who it was taken from.' where id = '9005c132-f729-5b6c-949f-226c4f1a2c52' and body_md = '| **me** robaron | they robbed me |
| **te** robaron | they robbed you |
| **le** robaron a mi vieja | they robbed my mom |
| **nos** robaron la bici | they stole our bike |
| **me** afanaron, **me** estafaron | they swiped it, they scammed me |
The verb stays *robaron*; the pronoun in front says who lost out.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Among friends it''s **me afanaron** — *they stole it* (slang) — with the same *they* that nobody names. It moves with the victim: **te robaron**, **le robaron a mi vieja**, **nos robaron la bici**. The **motochorro** does it from a motorbike.' where id = '9f1b4f75-62bb-5fd3-bfb4-117dc43f4612' and body_md = 'Among friends it''s **me afanaron** — *they swiped it* — with the same *they* that nobody names. It moves with the victim: **te robaron**, **le robaron a mi vieja**, **nos robaron la bici**. The **motochorro** does it from a motorbike.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Living in a building means paying **expensas** — *the monthly building fees* — to the **consorcio** — *the owners'' association*. The **encargado** is the building caretaker, and knows everything.' where id = '91a5e921-8540-53dc-904c-1b0a1d6a8502' and body_md = 'Living in a building means paying **expensas** — *the monthly building fees* — to the **consorcio**. The **encargado** is the building caretaker, and knows everything.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Each problem has its person: the **plomero** for a **canilla** that **gotea** — *a dripping faucet* — the **gasista** for the calefón, the **encargado** for the **portero eléctrico**. A **filtración** from the apartment upstairs goes to the **administración** — *the management office* — and takes months.' where id = 'e7c5b8b2-bd38-57ba-bd75-9d14c7757dc8' and body_md = 'Each problem has its person: the **plomero** for a **canilla** that **gotea** — *a dripping faucet* — the **gasista** for the calefón, the **encargado** for the **portero eléctrico**. A **filtración** from the apartment upstairs goes to the **administración**, and takes months.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'To go to the **estadio** you''re **socio** — *a member* — of the **club**, and pay the cuota. The **hinchada** sings its **cantitos** for ninety minutes, under the **banderas**. Away fans? Mostly banned since 2013: you usually only go **de visitante** on TV.' where id = 'bcc20295-b0f0-5657-8bba-544e8abc8f78' and body_md = 'To go to the **estadio** you''re **socio** — *a member* — of the **club**, and pay the cuota. The **hinchada** sings its **cantitos** for ninety minutes, under the **banderas**. Away fans? Banned for years: you only go **de visitante** on TV.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteños grew up on **rock nacional** — *Argentine rock* — sung in Spanish in the stadiums; the provinces on **folclore**; every party ends in **cumbia**. A **cantante** is a singer; a tango singer is often called a *cantor*.' where id = '968d241f-9d2a-5644-9eff-acf620874f77' and body_md = 'Porteños grew up on **rock nacional** — *Argentine rock* — sung in Spanish in the stadiums; the provinces on **folclore**; every party ends in **cumbia**. A **cantante** is a singer; the one who sings tango is a *cantor*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'For the table there''s the **parrillada** — *a mixed grill* on its own little grill: chorizo, morcilla, **mollejas** — *sweetbreads: a soft gland, not bread* — **chinchulines** and a **tira de asado**. On your own: a **bife de chorizo** or an **entraña**.' where id = '320ccab5-810e-5019-b4e8-625dde6a8ac3' and body_md = 'For the table there''s the **parrillada** — *a mixed grill* on its own little grill: chorizo, morcilla, **mollejas**, **chinchulines** and a **tira de asado**. On your own: a **bife de chorizo** or an **entraña**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me afanaron la billetera**, **me estafaron**; **se tapó la pileta**, **se trabó el ascensor** — with **me afanaron**, *they* did it and we don''t say who; with **se tapó**, it happened by itself and nobody did it.' where id = 'cab9d500-1ea5-50a6-b22b-98ddbe3c2137' and body_md = '**Me afanaron la billetera**, **me estafaron**; **se tapó la pileta**, **se trabó el ascensor** — the *they* nobody names, and the *se* nobody did.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Lo lindo** es que siempre hay algo. | The nice thing is there''s always something. |
| **Lo feo** es el tránsito. | The ugly part is the traffic. |
| **Lo difícil** fue el idioma. | The hard part was the language. |
| **Lo único** que extraño es el mar. | The only thing I miss is the sea. |
| **Lo más** lindo es la plaza del barrio. | The nicest thing is the local square. |

**Lo** + adjective makes *the … thing*, and **lo** never becomes la, los or las. With a plural noun, the verb is plural: **lo feo son los precios**.' where id = '7ae297c7-20ed-5a6a-976d-9efc0c4c19d4' and body_md = '| **Lo lindo** es que siempre hay algo. | The nice thing is there''s always something. |
| **Lo feo** es el tránsito. | The ugly part is the traffic. |
| **Lo difícil** fue el idioma. | The hard part was the language. |
| **Lo único** que extraño es el mar. | The only thing I miss is the sea. |
| **Lo más** lindo es la plaza del barrio. | The nicest thing is the local square. |

**Lo** + adjective makes *the … thing*, and it never changes: *lo lindo*, even of a plural.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Lo bueno** es la gente. | The good thing is the people. |
| **Lo malo** es el tránsito. | The bad thing is the traffic. |
| **Lo mejor** fue el asado. | The best part was the asado. |
| **Lo peor** es el calor. | The worst part is the heat. |
**Lo** + adjective makes *the … thing*, and **de** says of what: **lo peor de Buenos Aires**, **lo bueno de vivir acá es que…** **Lo** never becomes la, los or las. With a plural noun, the verb is plural: **lo malo son los precios**.' where id = '45734591-aa5f-52b7-bd71-165c7e2e5b2b' and body_md = '| **Lo bueno** es la gente. | The good thing is the people. |
| **Lo malo** es el tránsito. | The bad thing is the traffic. |
| **Lo mejor** fue el asado. | The best part was the asado. |
| **Lo peor** es el calor. | The worst part is the heat. |
**Lo** + adjective makes *the … thing*, and **de** says of what: **lo peor de Buenos Aires**, **lo bueno de vivir acá es que…** It never changes: *lo bueno*, even of a plural.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Nobody wants to **quedar mal** — *look rude*. So you thank them for the **invitación**, blame a **compromiso** — *a prior commitment* — and leave the door open: **la próxima voy**, **otro día**. And if they push: **no insistas, che**.' where id = 'cc5e231d-b0ac-5861-be50-d1802854aad9' and body_md = 'Nobody wants to **quedar mal** — *come off as rude*. So you thank them for the **invitación**, blame a **compromiso** — *a prior commitment* — and leave the door open: **la próxima voy**, **otro día**. And if they push: **no insistas, che**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'With *we*: **si hubiéramos salido antes, ya estaríamos ahí**. The participles: **ahorrado, comprado, vendido, aceptado**. **Hubiera** + participle also works alone as *would have*: **nunca lo hubiera vendido** — *I''d never have sold it*; **yo que vos, no lo hubiera vendido**. With *vos* it is **hubieras**: **¿lo hubieras vendido?** And **ojalá hubiera** + participle = *I wish I had*: **ojalá hubiera ahorrado más**.' where id = 'fdea7949-7c65-5ef1-92db-aafc9dc74362' and body_md = 'With *we*: **si hubiéramos salido antes, ya estaríamos ahí**. The participles: **ahorrado, comprado, vendido, aceptado**. **Hubiera** + participle also works alone as *would have*: **nunca lo hubiera vendido** — *I''d never have sold it*; **yo que vos, no lo hubiera vendido**.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'It works on adverbs too: **cerquita** — *close by*; **despacito** — *nice and slow*. **Chiquito** — *small, little*.' where id = '9c22a7d9-d890-5e17-a088-75954c74be37' and body_md = 'It works on adverbs too: **cerquita** — *really close*; **despacito** — *nice and slow*. **Chiquito** — *tiny*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**-ito** makes things small, and requests smaller: **un ratito** — *a little while*; **un cafecito**; **un poquito**. It sounds kind rather than childish.' where id = '492ceddb-7a1b-5bbd-9bdf-da57d4115735' and body_md = '**-ito** makes things small, and requests smaller: **un ratito** — *a sec*; **un cafecito**; **un poquito**. It sounds kind rather than childish.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Tendría que haber** ido. | I should have gone. |
| **Tendrías que haber** avisado. | You should have let us know. |
| **Me arrepiento.** | I regret it. |

**Tendría que haber** + participle: how porteños say *should have*. **Debería haber ido** is also correct, but sounds more formal.' where id = '04312d09-ee63-5a2e-aa3d-bac2d25e0910' and body_md = '| **Tendría que haber** ido. | I should have gone. |
| **Tendrías que haber** avisado. | You should have let us know. |
| **Me arrepiento.** | I regret it. |

**Tendría que haber** + participle: the porteño regret. Never *he debido*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'With *vos*: **¿te arrepentís?**; with *him*: **se arrepintió**. **Dejé pasar la oportunidad** — *I let the chance go*. **Te lo perdiste** — *you missed out*. **Metí la pata** — *I made a mistake, I said or did the wrong thing*. **Lamentablemente**, you can''t **volver atrás**.' where id = '54279426-a9ab-597a-90c9-2ebc30ce6253' and body_md = 'With *vos*: **¿te arrepentís?**; with *him*: **se arrepintió**. A chance you **dejaste pasar** — *let slip* — gets a **te lo perdiste** from your friends; a blunder is **metí la pata**. **Lamentablemente**, you can''t **volver atrás**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Tendría que haber** ido. | I should have gone. |
| **Tendrías que haber** avisado. | You should have let me know. |
| **Tendríamos que haber** salido antes. | We should have left earlier. |
| **Tendrían que haber** llamado. | They should have called. |
| **Me hubiera gustado** verte. | I''d have liked to see you. |

And the feeling: **me arrepiento**, **¿te arrepentís?**, **se arrepintió**.' where id = '889cd02b-5ff9-579f-8a2e-b8fa444082c1' and body_md = '| **Tendría que haber** ido. | I should have gone. |
| **Tendrías que haber** avisado. | You should have said. |
| **Tendríamos que haber** salido antes. | We should have left earlier. |
| **Tendrían que haber** llamado. | They should have called. |
| **Me hubiera gustado** verte. | I''d have liked to see you. |

And the feeling: **me arrepiento**, **¿te arrepentís?**, **se arrepintió**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**A esta altura** — *by now* — goes in the *now* half of the sentence: **si me hubiera mudado a Córdoba, a esta altura estaría re tranquilo**. New participles: **mudado, aprendido, dejado, invertido**.' where id = '5a7bee24-001f-5d37-813f-64d1da9b1600' and body_md = '**A esta altura** — *by now* — is how porteños bring the other life into the present: **si me hubiera mudado a Córdoba, a esta altura estaría re tranquilo**. New participles: **mudado, aprendido, dejado, invertido**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**No es que no quiera** (subjunctive: not the real reason), **es que no puedo** (normal present: the real reason).' where id = 'b7616641-58f0-580f-9dfb-573e381cdbf5' and body_md = '**No es que no quiera** (subjunctive), **es que no puedo** (normal verb).';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Words ending in *-r*, *-n*, *-e* take **-cito**: **calor → calorcito**, **café → cafecito**. Short *sol* does too: **solcito**. Words in *-o* just swap it for **-ito**, and a *c* turns *qu*: **fresco → fresquito**. Porteños love diminutives for nice weather: **hace fresquito**, **qué lindo calorcito**.' where id = '25238004-814b-58f4-824a-ded9fff9bc9e' and body_md = 'Words ending in *-r*, *-n*, *-e* take **-cito**: **calor → calorcito**, **café → cafecito**. Short *sol* does too: **solcito**. Words in *-o* just swap it for **-ito**, and a *c* turns *qu*: **fresco → fresquito**. Porteños talk about the weather almost only in diminutives: **hace fresquito**, **qué lindo calorcito**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo que pasa es que…** — *the thing is* — explains the real reason. **Lo raro es que…** — *the weird thing is*; **lo importante es que…** — *what matters is*. A fact takes the normal verb: **lo importante es que llegaste**. Something not real yet takes the subjunctive: **lo importante es que la pases bien**.' where id = '49e04ee1-475c-5da9-8fc8-72277c9ebf70' and body_md = '**Lo que pasa es que…** — *the thing is* — explains the real reason. **Lo raro es que…** — *the weird thing is*; **lo importante es que…** — *what matters is*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo de** is *the thing with*: **¿qué pasó con lo de Juan?** And **lo de siempre** is *the usual*: at the café, at the bar, in life.' where id = 'c6fee335-6750-566b-8494-37dd8682218f' and body_md = '**Lo de** is *the business with*: **¿qué pasó con lo de Juan?** And **lo de siempre** is *the usual*: at the café, at the bar, in life.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Lo** turns anything into *the thing*: **lo tuyo es la cocina** — *your thing is cooking*; **lo mío** — *my thing*; **lo primero** — *the first thing*; **lo justo** — *just enough*. Giving up an argument: **lo que vos digas** — *whatever you say*. **Lo que sea** — *whatever, anything*: **comemos lo que sea**.' where id = 'e19109d4-b42a-551e-8023-98c286a43783' and body_md = '**Lo** turns anything into *the thing*: **lo tuyo es la cocina** — *your thing is cooking*; **lo mío** — *my thing*; **lo primero** — *the first thing*; **lo justo** — *just enough*. Giving up an argument: **lo que vos digas** or **lo que sea** — *whatever*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A **dicho** is a saying, and porteños drop one to close an argument: **más vale tarde que nunca**; **no hay mal que por bien no venga** — *something good can come from something bad*.' where id = 'f3b9bf7b-1ef2-5454-ad89-23929822b1a5' and body_md = 'A **dicho** is a saying, and porteños drop one to close an argument: **más vale tarde que nunca**; **no hay mal que por bien no venga** — *every cloud has a silver lining*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Como dice el dicho** — *as the saying goes* — and then the one that fits: **cada loco con su tema** — *to each their own*; **no hay dos sin tres** — *it happened twice, it''ll happen again*; **el que no llora no mama** — *if you don''t ask, you don''t get*.' where id = 'a52eadb9-c139-52a4-b142-3865a13646ae' and body_md = '**Como dice el dicho** — *as the saying goes* — and then the one that fits: **cada loco con su tema** — *to each their own*; **no hay dos sin tres** — *it happened twice, it''ll happen again*; **el que no llora no mama** — *the squeaky wheel gets the grease*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Más vale pájaro en mano que cien volando** — *one sure thing is better than a hundred possible ones*; **a caballo regalado no se le miran los dientes** — *you don''t complain about a gift*; **ojos que no ven, corazón que no siente** — *what you don''t know can''t hurt you*; **del dicho al hecho hay mucho trecho** — *easier said than done*. **El que se quema con leche, ve una vaca y llora** — *after a bad experience, you''re scared of anything similar*. And when someone walks in: **hablando del rey de Roma…** — *we were just talking about you*' where id = 'c856ee20-16fd-55e2-88a7-bb617e0c577d' and body_md = '**Más vale pájaro en mano que cien volando** — *a bird in the hand*; **a caballo regalado no se le miran los dientes**; **ojos que no ven, corazón que no siente**; **del dicho al hecho hay mucho trecho** — *easier said than done*. **El que se quema con leche, ve una vaca y llora** — *once bitten, twice shy*. And when someone walks in: **hablando del rey de Roma…**';
update public.tips set body_md = '**El que avisa no traiciona** — *don''t say I didn''t warn you*. You say it while you give the warning. Literally: *the one who warns you doesn''t betray you*.' where id = 'e6b7166a-1ef7-5de5-90cc-d87a7c023771' and body_md = '**El que avisa no traiciona** — *I warned you*, literally *who warns doesn''t betray*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The **plazo** moves: they **postergaron la fecha** — *pushed the date back* — or, worse, **la adelantaron**. Then it''s **horas extra** until **entregamos** — *we hand it in* (also *we handed it in*). And the boss asks: **¿ya lo entregaste?**' where id = '667abe18-109e-562c-b974-4938f7888ca3' and body_md = 'The **plazo** moves: they **postergaron la fecha** — *pushed the date back* — or, worse, **la adelantaron**. Then it''s **horas extra** until **entregamos** — *we handed it in*. And the boss asks: **¿ya lo entregaste?**';
update public.tips set body_md = 'People get labels: a **rata** never pays; a **careta** is fake or uptight (or someone who doesn''t drink or party); **grasa** is tacky. **Estar manija** is to be very excited about something: **estoy manija con el recital**. The **cana** is the police. A friend who backs you **te hace la gamba**; one who talks nonsense **manda fruta**.' where id = '361c790d-a0af-59b6-8330-323cd924f6a0' and body_md = 'People get labels: a **rata** never pays; a **careta** is a square (or sober, or a phony); **grasa** is tacky. A **manija** is wound up about something: **estoy manija con el recital**. The **cana** is the police. A friend who backs you **te hace la gamba**; one who talks nonsense **manda fruta**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Me hizo** reír. | It made me laugh. |
| **Me hizo** sentir en casa. | It made me feel at home. |
| Vos **me hacés** reír. | You make me laugh. |
| **Nos hizo** llorar a todos. | It made us all cry. |

**Reírse**, now: me río, **te reís**, se ríe, nos reímos. Before: me reí, te reíste, **se rió**, nos reímos.' where id = 'e7e3983a-7d06-54c6-802c-1dea72caffff' and body_md = '| **Me hizo** reír. | It made me laugh. |
| **Me hizo** sentir en casa. | It made me feel at home. |
| Vos **me hacés** reír. | You make me laugh. |
| **Nos hizo** llorar a todos. | It made us all cry. |

**Reírse**: me reí, **te reís**, **se rió**, nos reímos.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Reírse** with *vos*: **¿de qué te reís?**; with *him*, in the past: **se rió** — *he laughed*. **¿Lloraste?** For the big laugh: **me morí de risa** — *I died laughing*. A **comedia** gets a **sonrisa**; a sad scene, **lágrimas** and **tristeza**. And people with **sentido del humor** laugh at themselves.' where id = '8b879baa-1e7b-5ea3-9967-18510251f924' and body_md = '**Reírse** with *vos*: **¿de qué te reís?**; with *him*: **se rió**. **¿Lloraste?** For the big laugh: **me morí de risa** — *I died laughing*. A **comedia** gets a **sonrisa**; a sad scene, **lágrimas** and **tristeza**. And people with **sentido del humor** laugh at themselves.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Chabón** — *guy*; **mina** — *woman*; **groso** — *great*; **birra** — *beer*; **trucho** — *fake*. All among friends.' where id = 'b5aa4be9-40fc-515c-b131-f7ba25d4134b' and body_md = '**Chabón**, **mina**, **groso**, **birra**, **trucho** — among friends.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Al horno** — *in trouble*; **qué bajón** — *what a shame*; **ni en pedo** — *no way*; **rata** — *stingy*; **careta** — *fake*; **manija** — *very excited*. All among friends.' where id = '2cdd21ad-467f-5fd7-a33c-ff457fb68650' and body_md = '**Al horno**, **qué bajón**, **ni en pedo**, **rata**, **careta**, **manija** — among friends.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Porteños are direct, but they soften it first: **sin ofender** — *no offense*; **te lo digo con cariño**; **no es nada personal**. A **crítica** goes down better that way, above all on a **tema delicado**.' where id = '102ea8d0-6e5a-50b1-816d-8bdb9e099e9b' and body_md = 'Porteños are direct, but they pad it: **sin ofender** — *no offense*; **te lo digo con cariño**; **no es nada personal**. A **crítica** goes down better that way, above all on a **tema delicado**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estamos atrasados** — *we''re behind*. The porteño answer: **no pasa nada, lo sacamos** — *it''s fine, we''ll get it done*.' where id = '4e18b4f7-e094-5c06-b878-27a365a546ec' and body_md = '**Estamos atrasados** — *we''re behind*. The porteño answer: **no pasa nada, lo sacamos**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '| **Me merezco** un aumento. | I deserve a raise. |
| **Me lo merezco.** | I deserve it. |
| **Te lo merecés.** | You deserve it. |
**Merecerse** usually comes with its pronoun in speech: the bare *merezco* is correct but more formal. And a boss who **valora** your work — *values* it — says so with the sueldo.' where id = '5f8b9622-8605-59be-9a2c-df64d8920c28' and body_md = '| **Me merezco** un aumento. | I deserve a raise. |
| **Me lo merezco.** | I deserve it. |
| **Te lo merecés.** | You deserve it. |
**Merecerse** comes with its pronoun: the bare *merezco* sounds like a textbook. And a boss who **valora** your work — *values* it — says so with the sueldo.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'Before you **negociar**, know what you''re owed. A job **en blanco** is *on the books*, with aguinaldo (an extra month''s pay) and obra social (health insurance); **en negro** is *off the books*. And with inflation, the regular **ajuste** — *the pay adjustment* — is the first thing you **exigir**.' where id = '906103c0-8825-51f0-8f33-0bb01926b4d9' and body_md = 'Before you **negociar**, know what you''re owed. A job **en blanco** is *on the books*, with aguinaldo and obra social; **en negro** is *off the books*. And with inflation, the yearly **ajuste** — *the pay adjustment* — is the first thing you **exigir**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me cayó la ficha** — *I finally understood* — comes from the old phone tokens that fell when the call went through. **Recién ahora me cayó la ficha** — *it only just sank in*.' where id = 'c4afb4c4-3d89-5295-aca0-b2a95d8259c6' and body_md = '**Me cayó la ficha** — *the penny dropped* — comes from the old phone tokens that fell when the call went through. **Recién ahora me cayó la ficha** — *it only just sank in*.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'In Argentina every Spaniard is a **gallego**, from Galicia or not. It is informal and friendly, but some Spaniards do not like it; the neutral word is **español**. And the great-grandparents still pay off: half of Buenos Aires is getting Italian or Spanish citizenship — **sacar la ciudadanía**. Your **raíces** — *roots* — come with a passport.' where id = '69083595-4dc0-5d7d-8816-d2abf4a0f8c7' and body_md = 'In Argentina every Spaniard is a **gallego**, from Galicia or not. And the great-grandparents still pay off: half of Buenos Aires is sacando **la ciudadanía** italiana or española. Your **raíces** — *roots* — come with a passport.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The **cordillera** — *the Andes range* — runs down the whole west: **lagos** and **nieve** in the south, **bodegas** — *wineries* — in Mendoza, red **valles** in Jujuy. A **mochilero** does it all with a backpack and a **carpa** — *a tent*, down to Ushuaia.' where id = 'b4d85210-f57c-504d-a015-0281e2125c5a' and body_md = 'The **cordillera** — *the Andes range* — runs down the whole west: **lagos** and **nieve** in the south, **bodegas** — *wineries* — in Mendoza, red **valles** in Jujuy. A **mochilero** does it all with a backpack and a carpa, down to Ushuaia.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Acampamos al lado de un lago**, **hicimos dedo**; **¿te convido un mate?** — but **no hiervas el agua**. On the beach, a **carpa** is a rented beach tent (a cabana).' where id = '9f9ceb73-2afc-50c6-b957-5e19f23e93c9' and body_md = '**Acampamos al lado de un lago**, **hicimos dedo**; **¿te convido un mate?** — but **no hiervas el agua**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me hace ruido**, **no me cierra**, **me quedé helado**, **qué alivio** — doubt, shock and relief, in porteño.' where id = 'a34223c2-0e77-5292-af66-2d1ef580ba10' and body_md = '**Me hace ruido**, **no me cierra**, **me quedé helado**, **qué alivio** — the gut, in porteño.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estar** + the **-ando / -iendo** form is how you catch a joke in progress: **me estás tomando el pelo** — *you''re joking with me*; **¿me estás jodiendo?** — *you''re kidding me*; **estás exagerando**. And when you believed it: **¡caíste!** — *got you!* — **qué inocente**. **Jodiendo** and **en joda** are very casual: fine with friends, not with a boss. Safer: **¿me estás cargando?**' where id = '6044efe3-ab79-5a6e-bf86-377632411a37' and body_md = '**Estar** + the **-ando / -iendo** form is how you catch a joke in progress: **me estás tomando el pelo** — *you''re pulling my leg*; **¿me estás jodiendo?** — *you''re kidding me*; **estás exagerando**. And when you believed it: **¡caíste!** — *got you!* — **qué inocente**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cargar** someone is *to tease, to joke with someone*: **¿me estás cargando?** — *are you joking with me?* Porteños **cargan** the people they like; being left alone is the bad sign.' where id = '598bffd2-cea9-5528-8b85-1bec66093ce9' and body_md = '**Cargar** someone is *to tease, to wind up*: **¿me estás cargando?** — *are you pulling my leg?* Porteños **cargan** the people they like; being left alone is the bad sign.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'The joke only works if you don''t **picarse** — *get touchy*: **se picó** is the worst thing to say about someone at an asado. Everybody has an **apodo** — *a nickname* — and a **broma** — *a prank* — is a sign of affection. **No te hagas el vivo**, though: **te hacés el vivo** is *you''re trying to be clever, to take advantage of someone*.' where id = 'a3dfd806-54f5-516a-a10e-12f1e87569d8' and body_md = 'The joke only works if you don''t **picarse** — *get touchy*: **se picó** is the worst thing to say about someone at an asado. Everybody has an **apodo** — *a nickname* — and a **broma** — *a prank* — is a sign of affection. **No te hagas el vivo**, though: **te hacés el vivo** is *you''re acting smart*.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Entregamos sobre la hora**, **postergaron la fecha**; **se lo merece**, **nos lo merecemos** — *he or she deserves it*, *we deserve it*.' where id = 'c4d61984-886d-5f1c-85e3-6db107bc6b5a' and body_md = '**Entregamos sobre la hora**, **postergaron la fecha**; **se lo merece**, **nos lo merecemos** — work, every person.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Estoy orgulloso de vos** — *I''m proud of you*. **Agradecido** — *grateful*: **estoy muy agradecida**. Grateful *to* a person: **agradecido con vos**. Grateful *for* a thing: **agradecida por el regalo**.' where id = '73a05d53-1c14-5efb-ad11-2e0630cff1d7' and body_md = '**Estoy orgulloso de vos** — *I''m proud of you*. **Agradecido** — *grateful*: **estoy muy agradecida**.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Me llegó** — *it really touched me*: **tu mensaje me llegó un montón**. Say it **de todo corazón**. **Sos un orgullo** — *you make us proud*. After the **discurso**, my dad **me abrazó** — *hugged me* — and the **felicidad** was all over the room.' where id = 'a25e7141-158e-5b98-ad99-7895076ecc1f' and body_md = '**Me llegó** — *it really touched me*: **tu mensaje me llegó un montón**. Say it **de todo corazón**. **Sos un orgullo** — *you make us proud*. After the **discurso**, everyone **se abrazó** — and the **felicidad** was all over the room.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Cargar** — *to tease*, **en joda** — *as a joke*, **me cayó la ficha** — *I finally understood* — humor, porteño style.' where id = '5571e01e-7110-522a-bd2f-bed64e49f2b0' and body_md = '**Cargar**, **en joda**, **un chiste gracioso** — humor, porteño style.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Se casó** — *got married*, **nació** — *was born*, **me emocioné** — *I got emotional* — the news that matters.' where id = '65ea12f5-9f24-5b33-96b2-d70a5923a81c' and body_md = '**Se casó**, **nació**, **me emocioné** — the news that matters.';
update public.tips set body_md = '**Te estaba tomando el pelo**, **¡caíste!**, **no te piques** — teasing someone, porteño style: *I was joking with you*, *you believed it!*, *don''t get offended*.' where id = '72041628-e505-5055-893b-2971932a487a' and body_md = '**Te estaba tomando el pelo**, **¡caíste!**, **no te piques** — the wind-up, in porteño.';
update public.tips set body_md = 'A porteño **despedida** — *farewell party* — ends with a toast: **¡brindemos!**, **brindo por ustedes**. Then **gracias por todo**, **fue un placer**, and never *adiós*: you say **chau** or **hasta la próxima**, because here nobody really leaves. **Me despido de todos** — *I''m saying goodbye to everyone*.' where id = 'cf2878f8-b900-509f-b7ce-8ab38a91c757' and body_md = 'A porteño **despedida** — *farewell party* — ends with a toast: **¡brindemos!**, **brindo por ustedes**. Then **gracias por todo**, **fue un placer**, and never *adiós*: **me despido** with **hasta la próxima**, because here nobody really leaves.';
